</html>","i":"","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.landian.news/archives/126543.html":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"content-post\">\n                <p class=\"excerpt color-border color-bg\">#行业资讯 Linux 内核基础设施遭到 AI 爬虫持续轰炸，即便部署反爬措施现在也会被 AI 爬虫绕过。Linux 基金会 IT 基础设施负责人兼内核设施管理员里亚比采夫日前透露内核基础设施遭到持续轰炸，每天 600 万次请求里只有 2% 是正常访问。即便现在已经部署 Anubis 工作量证明验证机制，AI 爬虫也可以继续绕过。查看全文：https://ourl.co/126543</p><p>Linux Foundation IT 基础设施负责人兼内核设施管理员康斯坦丁・里亚比采夫近日公布 git.kernel.org 的实际流量数据，直言 AI 时代的网络爬虫已经成为长期基础设施负担。</p>\n<p>需要说明的是这并非 Linux 基金会发布的官方政策声明，而是负责 IT 基础设施的管理员基于服务器数据给出的观察，目前 Linux 基金会还未说明要禁止 AI 爬虫抓取内容或实施其他政策。</p>\n<p><strong></strong></p>\n<p>目前内核 Git 每天约收到 600 万次随机提交页面请求，其中 66% 的请求会被 Anubis 工作量证明验证机制拦截，该验证机制会在访问者设备上进行少量 CPU 计算以证实这是真实人类访问，不过目前已经有 33% 的请求可以完成验证继续访问。</p>\n<p>里亚比采夫估算，即便采用比较宽松的判断标准，真正的正常访问可能也只有 2%。在分布于 5 个节点的 90 个 CPU 核心中，长期有 14~16 个核心专门用于把 Git 提交渲染为 HTML 供这些爬虫抓取，这消耗大约 20% 的算力，消耗甚至超过 Git 克隆等其他正常访问。</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://img.lancdn.com/landian/2026/08/126543.png\" data-fancybox=\"gallery\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-126567 size-full\" src=\"https://img.lancdn.com/landian/2026/08/126543.png\" alt=\"Linux内核基础设施遭到AI爬虫持续轰炸 即便部署反爬措施也会被AI绕过\"></a></p>\n<p><strong></strong></p>\n<p>里亚比采夫称 Linux 内核仓库天然适合训练模型：历史代码和提交记录公开，并且大量内容产生于生成式 AI 普及前，因此这些内容可以作为相对干净的训练语料。</p>\n<p>问题在于数据本来可以直接通过 Git 高效克隆，但部分爬虫选择逐个请求 cgit 生成的 HTML 页面。Linux 内核主仓库约有 148 万个提交，但 git.kernel.org 还有约 922 个相关分支仓库，同一批 Git 对象由此可以组合出数十亿甚至更多有效的 URL，大量重复抓取反而将渲染压力全部留给服务器。</p>\n<p><strong></strong></p>\n<p>早期爬虫还会暴露 UA 或集中使用云服务器 IP，管理员可以通过 fail2ban、封锁 IP 地址或 IP 所属的 ASN 自治网络来实施高效封禁。后来流量开始大量来自住宅 IP 和移动网络 IP 代理，每个地址仅请求数次后便消失。</p>\n<p>同时爬虫伪装为普通浏览器，里亚比采夫认为这与代理 SDK 变现网络有关，此前三星和 LG 电视都会被发现有大量第三方应用内含代理 SDK，将用户网络变成代理 IP 走流量。</p>\n<p>随后里亚比采夫部署 Anubis 验证机制，要求访问者完成工作量证明，最初这确实有效果，但现在爬虫逐渐可以完成难度 4 甚至 5 的验证，而继续提高难度又会让手机等正常用户等待更久并增加计算负担，所以也无法继续提高难度。</p>\n<p>目前 Linux 基础设施并未被这些流量压垮，但管理员已经准备减少可抓取的 URL、关闭部分高成本功能、对匿名访问增加限制等。真正的问题并非公开数据抓取，而是爬虫利用效率极低的方式反复消耗开放源码社区有限的基础设施资源，最终代价可能由所有正常用户共同承担。</p>\n<p><strong></strong></p>\n<article class=\"post-card post-list-main list color-bg color-border module-radius post simple\"><div class=\"list-content\"><p><a href=\"https://www.landian.news/archives/110330.html\" title=\"美国CDN提供商Fastly发布25Q2威胁报告 报告显示80%的流量都来自AI爬虫而不是真人\" class=\"title\"><h3>美国CDN提供商Fastly发布25Q2威胁报告 报告显示80%的流量都来自AI爬虫而不是真人</h3></a></p><p class=\"excerpt color-text\">#行业资讯 美国 CDN 提供商 Fastly 发布 25Q2 威胁报告，报告显示 80% 的流量来自 AI 爬虫，但这还不是最可怕的：可怕的是…</p><p class=\"post-metas color-meta\"><span title=\"文章分类\" class=\"tooltip top category iconfont icon-category\"><a href=\"https://www.landian.news/tech\" class=\"color-meta\">科技资讯</a>, <a href=\"https://www.landian.news/tech/industry\" class=\"color-meta\">行业资讯</a></span><span title=\"发布日期\" class=\"tooltip top date iconfont icon-date\">2025年8月21日 17:19</span><span class=\"separate\"></span><span title=\"浏览数量\" class=\"tooltip top view iconfont icon-view\">17.66K</span></p></div></article>\n<article class=\"post-card post-list-main list color-bg color-border module-radius post simple\"><div class=\"list-content\"><p><a href=\"https://www.landian.news/archives/109702.html\" title=\"自由软件基金会FSF遭到持续DDoS攻击 还被各大AI公司的爬虫狂轰滥炸\" class=\"title\"><h3>自由软件基金会FSF遭到持续DDoS攻击 还被各大AI公司的爬虫狂轰滥炸</h3></a></p><p class=\"excerpt color-text\">#行业资讯 自由软件基金会 FSF 发文称遭到持续性 DDoS 攻击，攻击持续时间已经快 1 年还没有停止。除了常规的 DDoS 攻击外，FSF…</p><p class=\"post-metas color-meta\"><span title=\"文章分类\" class=\"tooltip top category iconfont icon-category\"><a href=\"https://www.landian.news/tech\" class=\"color-meta\">科技资讯</a>, <a href=\"https://www.landian.news/tech/industry\" class=\"color-meta\">行业资讯</a></span><span title=\"发布日期\" class=\"tooltip top date iconfont icon-date\">2025年7月8日 14:11</span><span class=\"separate\"></span><span title=\"浏览数量\" class=\"tooltip top view iconfont icon-view\">14.05K</span></p></div></article>\n<article class=\"post-card post-list-main list color-bg color-border module-radius post simple\"><div class=\"list-content\"><p><a href=\"https://www.landian.news/archives/108610.html\" title=\"维基百科附属的维基媒体被AI爬虫轰炸 超过65%的昂贵网络流量由AI爬虫消耗\" class=\"title\"><h3>维基百科附属的维基媒体被AI爬虫轰炸 超过65%的昂贵网络流量由AI爬虫消耗</h3></a></p><p class=\"excerpt color-text\">#科技资讯 维基百科的附属项目维基媒体遭到 AI 爬虫的轰炸， 超过 65% 的昂贵网络流量被 AI 爬虫消耗，整体下载带宽增长 50% 而且都…</p><p class=\"post-metas color-meta\"><span title=\"文章分类\" class=\"tooltip top category iconfont icon-category\"><a href=\"https://www.landian.news/tech\" class=\"color-meta\">科技资讯</a>, <a href=\"https://www.landian.news/tech/industry\" class=\"color-meta\">行业资讯</a></span><span title=\"发布日期\" class=\"tooltip top date iconfont icon-date\">2025年4月3日 09:28</span><span class=\"separate\"></span><span title=\"浏览数量\" class=\"tooltip top view iconfont icon-view\">12.03K</span></p></div></article>\n<article class=\"post-card post-list-main list color-bg color-border module-radius post simple\"><div class=\"list-content\"><p><a href=\"https://www.landian.news/archives/108486.html\" title=\"Cloudflare推出AI迷宫功能 通过生成海量无关内容将爬虫放进迷宫里避免抓取网站\" class=\"title\"><h3>Cloudflare推出AI迷宫功能 通过生成海量无关内容将爬虫放进迷宫里避免抓取网站</h3></a></p><p class=\"excerpt color-text\">#人工智能 Cloudflare 推出 AI 迷宫功能，通过生成海量无关内容将爬虫放到迷宫里避免抓取网站正常内容。该功能算是以毒攻毒，检测到异常…</p><p class=\"post-metas color-meta\"><span title=\"文章分类\" class=\"tooltip top category iconfont icon-category\"><a href=\"https://www.landian.news/tech/ai\" class=\"color-meta\">人工智能</a>, <a href=\"https://www.landian.news/tech\" class=\"color-meta\">科技资讯</a></span><span title=\"发布日期\" class=\"tooltip top date iconfont icon-date\">2025年3月23日 10:47</span><span class=\"separate\"></span><span title=\"浏览数量\" class=\"tooltip top view iconfont icon-view\">14.82K</span></p></div></article>\n<article class=\"post-card post-list-main list color-bg color-border module-radius post simple\"><div class=\"list-content\"><p><a href=\"https://www.landian.news/archives/107504.html\" title=\"人体3D模型网站遭OpenAI爬虫疯狂抓取引起瘫痪 类似发起某种DDoS攻击\" class=\"title\"><h3>人体3D模型网站遭OpenAI爬虫疯狂抓取引起瘫痪 类似发起某种DDoS攻击</h3></a></p><p class=\"excerpt color-text\">#人工智能 乌克兰 3D 人体模型网站遭到 OpenAI 爬虫高频次抓取引发服务器弹簧，GPTBot 使用 600 多个 IP 发起数以万计的请…</p><p class=\"post-metas color-meta\"><span title=\"文章分类\" class=\"tooltip top category iconfont icon-category\"><a href=\"https://www.landian.news/tech/ai\" class=\"color-meta\">人工智能</a>, <a href=\"https://www.landian.news/tech\" class=\"color-meta\">科技资讯</a></span><span title=\"发布日期\" class=\"tooltip top date iconfont icon-date\">2025年1月12日 17:33</span><span class=\"separate\"></span><span title=\"浏览数量\" class=\"tooltip top view iconfont icon-view\">13.27K</span></p></div></article>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>消息源：</strong><a href=\"https://www.landian.news/go?url=https://people.kernel.org/monsieuricon/creepy-crawlies\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Kernel.org</a></p>\n<p class=\"single-activity-ticker\" aria-label=\"热门推荐\"><a class=\"single-activity-link\" href=\"https://www.landian.news/archives/114184.html\" title=\"仅需99元/年，硅谷CN2GIA服务器，另有3年版仅需528元，限量销售，售完即止\"><span class=\"single-activity-label\">热门推荐</span><span class=\"single-activity-window\"><span class=\"single-activity-track\"><span class=\"single-activity-title\">仅需99元/年，硅谷CN2GIA服务器，另有3年版仅需528元，限量销售，售完即止</span><span class=\"single-activity-title\" aria-hidden=\"true\">仅需99元/年，硅谷CN2GIA服务器，另有3年版仅需528元，限量销售，售完即止</span></span></span></a></p>            </div>\n        </div></body></html>","i":"","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.landian.news/archives/126542.html":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"content-post\">\n                <p class=\"excerpt color-border color-bg\">#行业资讯 Debian 项目组经过讨论和投票决定：既不鼓励使用 AI 生成代码，但也不禁止使用 AI 生成代码。如果贡献者使用 AI 生成代码，则必须能理解、审查和测试相关内容，在必要时还需要自行修改。AI 生成内容不会获得任何特殊豁免，开发者需要自行考虑 AI 输出的来源和潜在版权问题。查看全文：https://ourl.co/126542</p><p><a href=\"https://www.landian.news/archives/114101.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Debian 项目组此前围绕生成式 AI 使用政策进行投票</a>，经过讨论和正式投票后现在适用于 Debian 项目的负责任使用生成式 AI 方案胜出，这意味着 Debian 不会全面禁止开发者使用生成式 AI 参与项目。</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://img.lancdn.com/landian/2026/07/114101.png\" data-fancybox=\"gallery\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone\" src=\"https://img.lancdn.com/landian/2026/07/114101.png\" alt=\"Debian项目组完成AI使用政策投票 不鼓励使用AI但也不禁止使用AI\"></a></p>\n<p><strong></strong></p>\n<p>本次投票胜出的第 5 项方案明确表示，Debian 项目组不认可或推荐生成式 AI 工具，但也不禁止使用生成式 AI 工具。AI 可以用于软件开发、软件包维护、文档以及其他 Debian 项目工作，但无论什么工具，提交内容都必须达到相同的质量、正确性、可维护性和法律合规标准。</p>\n<p><strong></strong></p>\n<p>新政策的核心并不是允许开发者直接复制 AI 输出，而是将责任明确留给提交者本人。使用 AI 辅助生成代码或文档后，贡献者必须能够理解、审查和测试相关内容，在必要时还需要自行修改。盲目接受 AI 输出并直接上传，与 Debian 现有的开发规范不符。</p>\n<p>同时 AI 不会获得任何特殊豁免，现有的 DFSG、版权、许可证和软件自由要求仍然适用，开发者需要自行考虑 AI 输出的来源和潜在版权问题。Debian 项目组鼓励贡献者披露 AI 辅助使用情况，但目前不强制要求声明内容由 AI 生成。</p>\n<p><strong></strong></p>\n<p>新政策还特别强调数据安全问题，Debian 贡献者不得随意向第三方 AI 服务提交未公开讨论、个人信息、尚未披露的安全漏洞、密码、 密钥以及其他敏感项目资料。</p>\n<p>利用 AI 进行大规模错误报告、批量提交补丁、自动修改大量软件包等操作，仍然需要提前与社区讨论并取得共识，相关自动化流程也必须由具体人员监督并承担相应责任。</p>\n<p><strong></strong></p>\n<article class=\"post-card post-list-main list color-bg color-border module-radius post simple\"><div class=\"list-content\"><p><a href=\"https://www.landian.news/archives/114101.html\" title=\"Debian社区讨论是否禁止使用AI提交代码：有要求全面禁止 也有主张允许但必须披露\" class=\"title\"><h3>Debian社区讨论是否禁止使用AI提交代码：有要求全面禁止 也有主张允许但必须披露</h3></a></p><p class=\"excerpt color-text\">#人工智能 Debian 社区正在讨论是否禁止使用 AI 提交代码和其他贡献：已有提案要求全面禁止，也有提案主张允许但贡献者必须承担责任并进行披…</p><p class=\"post-metas color-meta\"><span title=\"文章分类\" class=\"tooltip top category iconfont icon-category\"><a href=\"https://www.landian.news/tech/ai\" class=\"color-meta\">人工智能</a>, <a href=\"https://www.landian.news/tech\" class=\"color-meta\">科技资讯</a></span><span title=\"发布日期\" class=\"tooltip top date iconfont icon-date\">2026年7月28日 10:00</span><span class=\"separate\"></span><span title=\"浏览数量\" class=\"tooltip top view iconfont icon-view\">4.65K</span></p></div></article>\n<p class=\"single-activity-ticker\" aria-label=\"热门推荐\"><a class=\"single-activity-link\" href=\"https://www.landian.news/archives/114184.html\" title=\"仅需99元/年，硅谷CN2GIA服务器，另有3年版仅需528元，限量销售，售完即止\"><span class=\"single-activity-label\">热门推荐</span><span class=\"single-activity-window\"><span class=\"single-activity-track\"><span class=\"single-activity-title\">仅需99元/年，硅谷CN2GIA服务器，另有3年版仅需528元，限量销售，售完即止</span><span class=\"single-activity-title\" aria-hidden=\"true\">仅需99元/年，硅谷CN2GIA服务器，另有3年版仅需528元，限量销售，售完即止</span></span></span></a></p>            </div>\n        </div></body></html>","i":"","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://workspaces.beehiiv.com/p/533-tiancheng-luo":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"_10pdwo80 dream-post-content-doc\"><div class=\"_1gqvddm0\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Tiancheng Luo (aka bbbigdear) is a product designer and tech and lifestyle creator focused on workspace aesthetics, modern living, and thoughtfully designed technology. Through cinematic storytelling and hands-on product exploration, he shares tools and objects that blend functionality with visual design.</span></p></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What are some of the main items in your workspace?</span></h2></p><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What is the most recent item that you've added to your workspace?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">The most recent addition to my workspace is an </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://workspacesxyz.link/LShaped\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">L-shaped standing desk from Vernal</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">. It completely changed the atmosphere of my setup, giving me more space to separate different types of work while making the whole environment feel more organized.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What is one change you'd like to make to your current workspace?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">I’d love for my workspace to feel calmer and more intentional. Not just on the desk surface, but in a more three-dimensional way. Right now, I feel like the wall space still needs more thoughtful design so the entire environment feels more cohesive and organized.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Walk us through your morning routine—what’s the first thing you do at your desk?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Turning on the speakers. That’s always the first thing I do. Music helps me naturally shift into work mode. After that, I usually check messages, organize ideas for the day, and slowly ease into filming or scripting.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What’s one productivity trick that actually works for you?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">I think everyone should eventually build their own unique workflow instead of trying to copy someone else’s. Right now, AI probably makes up around 30% of my studio workflow, so learning how to work with AI tools has become really important for me.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What’s the most underrated app or tool you use every day?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">ChatGPT. I think everyone’s ChatGPT becomes different over time. After months of conversations, it starts understanding you on a much deeper level. For me, it’s not just a tool anymore, but something that helps organize ideas, refine concepts, and challenge my thinking.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></body></html>","i":"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,quality=80,width=1200,onerror=redirect/uploads/asset/file/6c438768-b421-4d9b-87d8-065b787f5105/DSC00691.jpg?t=1781356255","t":"2026-09-02","p":"","n":0},"https://www.landian.news/archives/126540.html":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"content-post\">\n                <p class=\"excerpt color-border color-bg\">#游戏资讯 英伟达将在 10 月发布适用于 Windows 10 的最终版显卡驱动程序更新，之后将提供 3 年安全更新但不再提供任何新功能。对 Windows 10 游戏玩家来说升级 Windows 11 是有必要的，因为英伟达经常通过驱动程序更新优化和适配游戏。继续使用 Windows 10 将无法获得必要的游戏兼容更新，这可能会导致新游戏体验下降、已发行的游戏出现问题无法修复等。查看全文：https://ourl.co/126540</p><p>英伟达在 2024 年和 2025 年都已经提前预告显卡驱动程序将逐渐停止支持 Windows 10 系统，即如果玩家想要获得显卡驱动带来的最新功能，则必须升级 Windows 11 系统。</p>\n<p>根据计划英伟达将在 2026 年 10 月发布适用于 Windows 10 的最终版显卡驱动程序 (带功能更新的)，之后只提供安全维护更新，不再为 Windows 10 提供任何新功能或游戏优化等。</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://img.lancdn.com/landian/2025/01/107428.png\" data-fancybox=\"gallery\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone\" src=\"https://img.lancdn.com/landian/2025/01/107428.png\" alt=\"英伟达将在10月发布适用于Windows 10的最终版显卡驱动 之后停止功能更新\"></a></p>\n<p><strong></strong></p>\n<p>对游戏玩家而言英伟达的显卡驱动程序更新非常重要，因为英伟达、AMD 和英特尔通常都会与游戏开发商合作，在游戏发布前就提前通过驱动程序对游戏进行优化，这也是每次有新游戏发布前英伟达都会发布新版驱动程序的原因。</p>\n<p>而停止支持 Windows 10 意味着后续英伟达不再向用户提供带有最新功能的驱动程序更新，如果玩家想要玩新发布的游戏那就面临没有优化的窘境，这会导致游戏体验下降甚至出现运行问题。</p>\n<p>部分已经发行的游戏通常可以继续配合旧版驱动程序运行，不过有时候英伟达也需要通过驱动程序修复游戏兼容性问题，所以如果某个游戏有问题需要通过驱动程序修复，那 Windows 10 用户无法更新时同样会遇到体验问题。</p>\n<p><strong></strong></p>\n<p>按惯例英伟达也会继续为旧版系统提供 3 年安全更新，在 2026 年 10 月英伟达将发布适用于 Windows 10 的带有功能更新的最终版显卡驱动，从 2026 年 11 月开始英伟达只会面向 Windows 10 提供必要的安全更新 (如有)。</p>\n<p>安全更新截止日期为 2029 年 10 月，在此之前 Windows 10 用户仍然会收到更新，不过安全更新不一定每月都会发布，有时候英伟达可能 3~4 个月才会发布一个安全更新版本。</p>\n<hr>\n<p>消息源：<a href=\"https://www.landian.news/go?url=https://nvidia.custhelp.com/app/answers/detail/a_id/5695/~/geforce-support-plan-for-windows-10\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NVIDIA</a></p>\n<p class=\"single-activity-ticker\" aria-label=\"热门推荐\"><a class=\"single-activity-link\" href=\"https://www.landian.news/archives/114184.html\" title=\"仅需99元/年，硅谷CN2GIA服务器，另有3年版仅需528元，限量销售，售完即止\"><span class=\"single-activity-label\">热门推荐</span><span class=\"single-activity-window\"><span class=\"single-activity-track\"><span class=\"single-activity-title\">仅需99元/年，硅谷CN2GIA服务器，另有3年版仅需528元，限量销售，售完即止</span><span class=\"single-activity-title\" aria-hidden=\"true\">仅需99元/年，硅谷CN2GIA服务器，另有3年版仅需528元，限量销售，售完即止</span></span></span></a></p>            </div>\n        </div></body></html>","i":"","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.landian.news/archives/126539.html":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"content-post\">\n                <p class=\"excerpt color-border color-bg\">#ç³»ç»Ÿèµ„è®¯ Microsoft Defender å�ˆå‡ºé—®é¢˜ï¼šå�¯èƒ½ä¼šé¢‘ç¹�å¼¹å‡ºé˜²ç—…æ¯’è½¯ä»¶å·²å…³é—­çš„é€šçŸ¥ã€‚è¯¥é—®é¢˜ä¸�å¾®è½¯è¿‘æœŸæ�¨é€�çš„æ›´æ–°æœ‰å…³ (é˜²ç—…æ¯’è½¯ä»¶æ›´æ–°)ï¼Œè€Œé€šçŸ¥åˆ™å�¯èƒ½é¢‘ç¹�æˆ–é—´æ­‡æ€§å¼¹å‡ºï¼Œå�³ä¾¿å…³é—­é€šçŸ¥ä¹Ÿä¸�èƒ½å½»åº•æ¶ˆé™¤é€šçŸ¥ã€‚å¾®è½¯ç§°æ­£åœ¨åˆ¶å®šä¿®å¤�æ–¹æ¡ˆï¼Œå��ç»­è§£å†³é—®é¢˜å��å°†æ�¨é€�æ›´æ–°è¿›è¡Œä¿®å¤�ã€‚æŸ¥çœ‹å…¨æ–‡ï¼šhttps://ourl.co/126539</p><p>æ�®å¾®è½¯å�‘å¸ƒçš„æ”¯æŒ�æ–‡æ¡£ï¼Œå®‰è£…è¿‘æœŸ Microsoft Defender é˜²ç—…æ¯’è½¯ä»¶æœ€æ–°æ›´æ–°å��ï¼Œç³»ç»Ÿå�¯èƒ½ä¼šé¢‘ç¹�å¼¹å‡º Microsoft Defender é˜²ç—…æ¯’è½¯ä»¶å·²å…³é—­çš„é€šçŸ¥ã€‚</p>\n<p>ç›®å‰�çš„é—®é¢˜æ˜¯æ— è®º Microsoft Defender æ˜¯å�¦çœŸè¢«ç¦�ç”¨ï¼Œè¿™ä¸ªé€šçŸ¥éƒ½ä¼šé¢‘ç¹�å¼¹å‡ºï¼Œè€Œä¸”å�³ä¾¿ç”¨æˆ·å…³é—­é€šçŸ¥è®¾ç½®å��ï¼Œè¿™äº›é€šçŸ¥è¿˜ä¼šåƒ�ç‰›çš®ç™£é‚£æ ·ç»§ç»­å­˜åœ¨ã€‚</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://img.lancdn.com/landian/2024/06/104643.png\" data-fancybox=\"gallery\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone\" src=\"https://img.lancdn.com/landian/2024/06/104643.png\" alt=\"Microsoft Defenderå�ˆå‡ºé—®é¢˜ï¼šå�¯èƒ½ä¼šé¢‘ç¹�å¼¹å‡ºé˜²ç—…æ¯’è½¯ä»¶å·²å…³é—­çš„é€šçŸ¥\"></a></p>\n<p><strong><div class=\"message-box message-style module-radius error\"><p class=\"salong-message-content\"> å‡ ä¹�æ‰€æœ‰ç‰ˆæœ¬éƒ½å�—å½±å“�ï¼š</p></div></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows 11 26H1</li>\n<li>Windows11 25H2/24H2</li>\n<li>Windows 11 23H2</li>\n<li>Windows 10 22H2/21H2</li>\n<li>Windows 10 LTSC 2019/2016</li>\n<li>Windows Server 2012~2025 æ‰€æœ‰ç‰ˆæœ¬</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><div class=\"message-box message-style module-radius success\"><p class=\"salong-message-content\"> å¾®è½¯å°†åœ¨ä¿®å¤�å��æ�¨é€�æ›´æ–°ï¼š</p></div></strong></p>\n<p>ç›®å‰�å¾®è½¯æ­£åœ¨è°ƒæŸ¥é—®é¢˜å�‘ç”Ÿå�Ÿå› å’Œåˆ¶å®šä¿®å¤�æ–¹æ¡ˆï¼Œå½“å®Œæˆ�ä¿®å¤�æ–¹æ¡ˆåˆ¶å®šå��å¾®è½¯ä¼šé€šè¿‡è‡ªåŠ¨æ›´æ–°æ�¨é€�è§£å†³æ–¹æ¡ˆã€‚ç›®å‰�ä½¿ç”¨ Microsoft Defender çš„ç”¨æˆ·å�¯ä»¥å¿½ç•¥ç³»ç»Ÿé”™è¯¯å¼¹å‡ºçš„é€šçŸ¥ï¼Œç­‰å¾®è½¯ä¿®å¤�å��è¿™äº›é€šçŸ¥åº”è¯¥å°±ä¼šè‡ªåŠ¨æ¶ˆå¤±ã€‚</p>\n<p>æ³¨æ„�ï¼šæ­¤é—®é¢˜ä¸� Windows 11 æœˆåº¦ç´¯ç§¯æ›´æ–°æ— å…³ï¼Œå�¸è½½æ›´æ–°ä¸�èƒ½è§£å†³é—®é¢˜ã€‚</p>\n<hr>\n<p>æ¶ˆæ�¯æº�ï¼š<a href=\"https://www.landian.news/go?url=https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/release-health/status-windows-11-25h2#4956msgdesc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Microsoft Learn</a></p>\n<p class=\"single-activity-ticker\" aria-label=\"çƒ­é—¨æ�¨è��\"><a class=\"single-activity-link\" href=\"https://www.landian.news/archives/114184.html\" title=\"ä»…éœ€99å…ƒ/å¹´ï¼Œç¡…è°·CN2GIAæœ�åŠ¡å™¨ï¼Œå�¦æœ‰3å¹´ç‰ˆä»…éœ€528å…ƒï¼Œé™�é‡�é”€å”®ï¼Œå”®å®Œå�³æ­¢\"><span class=\"single-activity-label\">çƒ­é—¨æ�¨è��</span><span class=\"single-activity-window\"><span class=\"single-activity-track\"><span class=\"single-activity-title\">ä»…éœ€99å…ƒ/å¹´ï¼Œç¡…è°·CN2GIAæœ�åŠ¡å™¨ï¼Œå�¦æœ‰3å¹´ç‰ˆä»…éœ€528å…ƒï¼Œé™�é‡�é”€å”®ï¼Œå”®å®Œå�³æ­¢</span><span class=\"single-activity-title\" aria-hidden=\"true\">ä»…éœ€99å…ƒ/å¹´ï¼Œç¡…è°·CN2GIAæœ�åŠ¡å™¨ï¼Œå�¦æœ‰3å¹´ç‰ˆä»…éœ€528å…ƒï¼Œé™�é‡�é”€å”®ï¼Œå”®å®Œå�³æ­¢</span></span></span></a></p>            </div>\n        </div></body></html>","i":"","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.landian.news/archives/126538.html":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"content-post\">\n                <p class=\"excerpt color-border color-bg\">#人工智能 索尼音乐和华纳联合起诉 Anthropic，指控后者未经授权盗用受版权的歌曲歌词训练 Claude AI 模型。索尼和华纳还将 A 社首席执行官达里奥与 A 社联合创始人本杰明列为被告。索尼和华纳称 A 社通过 BT 和盗版下载站获取大量版权内容并将其中的歌词用于模型训练，索尼和华纳要求 A 社为每首被侵权的歌曲歌词赔偿 15 万美元。查看全文：https://ourl.co/126538</p><p>索尼音乐出版公司和华纳查佩尔音乐出版公司日前在美国加州法院起诉人工智能公司 Anthropic，指控该公司未经授权的情况下盗用受版权保护的音乐歌词训练人工智能模型。索尼和华纳还将 A 社首席执行官达里奥和 A 社联合创始人本杰明曼恩列为被告。</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://img.lancdn.com/landian/2025/05/109080-1.png\" data-fancybox=\"gallery\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone\" src=\"https://img.lancdn.com/landian/2025/05/109080-1.png\" alt=\"索尼音乐与华纳联合起诉Anthropic 指控其未经授权盗用大量歌词训练AI模型\"></a></p>\n<p><strong><div class=\"message-box message-style module-radius error\"><p class=\"salong-message-content\"> 通过 BT 等渠道下载大量版权内容用于训练 AI 模型：</p></div></strong></p>\n<p>索尼和华纳在诉状中表示，A 社通过 BT 以及各类盗版下载站下载和抓取大量版权内容，将其中的歌词用于 Claude AI 模型训练。这些内容不仅被复制并进入训练数据，Claude AI 模型还可能生成相同或相似度较高的歌词，从而构成持续侵权。</p>\n<p>原告要求进行陪审团审判，要求针对故意侵犯版权的每首作品赔偿最高 15 万美元，如果涉及删除版权管理信息则原告还可以提出额外索赔。由于被侵权的作品非常多，理论上说原告索赔规模可能高达数十亿美元。</p>\n<p><strong></strong></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.landian.news/archives/114026.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">这起案件与此前美国图书出版社和作家起诉 A 社侵权有明显关联</a>，A 社早前已经同意支付 15 亿美元与出版社和作家就使用盗版书籍训练 Claude AI 模型的集体诉讼达成和解，大部分作家已经接受和解，每本被侵权的图书可能可以获得最高 2000 美元的赔偿，少部分作家不同意和解准备单独进行起诉。</p>\n<p>新的音乐诉讼认为 A 社获取歌曲歌词时使用相同或类似的盗版数据库，因此即使 AI 训练本身能否构成合理使用仍然存在争议，通过非法来源获取的训练材料也可能成为独立的版权问题。</p>\n<p><strong></strong></p>\n<p>音乐出版社还获得值得关注的欧洲判例，在德国慕尼黑地区法院审理的 GEMA 起诉 OpenAI 案件中，法院认定模型内部记忆中受版权保护的歌词本身可以构成复制，模型输出歌词则可能属于向公众传播。</p>\n<p>法院同时认为，欧盟的文本和数据挖掘豁免条例并不能覆盖这种永久性记忆，而且相关豁免原则上要求训练方合法取得作品，该判决目前尚未生效，不过已经为生成式 AI 训练歌词的版权争议提供重要参考。</p>\n<p class=\"single-activity-ticker\" aria-label=\"热门推荐\"><a class=\"single-activity-link\" href=\"https://www.landian.news/archives/114184.html\" title=\"仅需99元/年，硅谷CN2GIA服务器，另有3年版仅需528元，限量销售，售完即止\"><span class=\"single-activity-label\">热门推荐</span><span class=\"single-activity-window\"><span class=\"single-activity-track\"><span class=\"single-activity-title\">仅需99元/年，硅谷CN2GIA服务器，另有3年版仅需528元，限量销售，售完即止</span><span class=\"single-activity-title\" aria-hidden=\"true\">仅需99元/年，硅谷CN2GIA服务器，另有3年版仅需528元，限量销售，售完即止</span></span></span></a></p>            </div>\n        </div></body></html>","i":"","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://nicenews.com/culture/dogs-working-security-london-waterloo-train-station/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"entry-content clear\" ast-blocks-layout=\"true\" itemprop=\"text\">\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>This article was originally written by Isobel Williams</em> <em>for SWNS — the U.K.’s largest independent news agency, providing globally relevant original, verified, and engaging content to the world’s leading media outlets.</em></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">London’s Waterloo station has become the first major train station in Britain to put dogs on regular security patrols, employing canine colleagues Riley, Buster, and Flo as part of a three-month trial to offer passengers increased safety assurance. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Like a real-world version of the animated kids’ show <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k9CTlUHNg_Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><em>Paw Patrol</em></a>, the pups were deployed by South Western Railway and Network Rail Wessex in partnership with canine security company Alpha Canine Specialists. And although we know they have very serious jobs, it’s hard not to break out in a grin when looking at their happy faces. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Riley, aged 11, and Buster, aged 9, are cocker spaniels, while Flo, aged 10, is a Labrador. This will be the trio’s final deployment before retirement. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/on-paw-trol-dog-1593926-890x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78646\" srcset=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/on-paw-trol-dog-1593926-890x1024.jpg 890w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/on-paw-trol-dog-1593926-261x300.jpg 261w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/on-paw-trol-dog-1593926-768x884.jpg 768w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/on-paw-trol-dog-1593926-1335x1536.jpg 1335w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/on-paw-trol-dog-1593926-1780x2048.jpg 1780w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 890px) 100vw, 890px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">SWR / NR Wessex / SWNS</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Intended to act as a visual deterrent for wrongdoers, the dogs are part of a wider program designed to keep railway customers and colleagues safe. Other recent measures include equipping staff with body-worn cameras, launching a CCTV upgrade, and investing in a dedicated outreach worker who engages with vulnerable young people around the station. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">“Security needs constant innovation and we’re taking positive steps to reassure our customers that we take their safety very seriously,” Dan Harrison, station manager at Waterloo, said in a South Western Rails <a href=\"https://www.southwesternrailway.com/other/news-and-media/news/2026/august/paws-on-patrol\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">news release</a>.</p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">He emphasized that the decision to add Riley, Buster, and Flo to the employee roster was a preventative measure. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-instagram wp-block-embed-instagram\">\n<blockquote class=\"instagram-media\" data-instgrm-captioned data-instgrm-permalink=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcgsxzaF8qP/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\" data-instgrm-version=\"14\"></blockquote></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">“Deploying these dogs is not linked to any increased threat. It’s simply part of providing more visual deterrence and offering our customers some additional reassurance,” Harrison said. “In the same way, we recently equipped all our colleagues with new hi-vis tabards to make them more easily identifiable to customers in the station who might need their help.”</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">While the new job duties might not be <em>quite</em> as thrilling as chasing birds off an airport runway like <a href=\"https://nicenews.com/environment/dogs-chase-birds-keep-airplanes-safe/\">these two border collies do in West Virginia</a>, getting adoring looks from passersby all day comes with its own benefits package.   </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">RELATED: <a href=\"https://nicenews.com/science/how-dogs-process-human-facial-expressions-smiles/\">What’s Going on Inside Your Dog’s Brain When You Smile at Them? Study Reveals How Pups Process Human Happiness</a></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t</div>\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/on-paw-trol-dog-1593927.jpg","t":"2026-09-02","p":"","n":0},"https://nicenews.com/humanity/teen-hugh-saetia-eternal-canvas-paints-portraits-grieving-families/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"entry-content clear\" ast-blocks-layout=\"true\" itemprop=\"text\">\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When Los Angeles-based high schooler Hugh Saetia was 6 years old, he experienced a loss most people don’t grapple with until they’re much older. His mother died. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Following her passing from gastrointestinal cancer, Saetia’s father hired a nanny named Marilyn McAllister to help care for his two sons, and the woman became a strong maternal presence in the boys’ lives. Tragically, around seven years later, in 2024, one of McAllister’s own sons was killed after his shift as a security guard in 2024. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-10-814x1024.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78632\" srcset=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-10-814x1024.png 814w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-10-239x300.png 239w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-10-768x966.png 768w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-10.png 1168w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 814px) 100vw, 814px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Courtesy of Hugh Saetia</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Saetia as a young child with Marilyn McAllister</em></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Saetia, then 14, yearned to help the woman who meant so much to him but was unsure how he could best support her. “I always loved art. I always loved paintings,” he told Nice News. “So my dad suggested that I maybe just do a painting of them.”</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">McAllister, who’d also lost her husband years earlier, followed by her youngest son, was deeply touched by the portrait. “There’s no words to express how I feel about it,” she said. “It’s beautiful. It’s beautiful work.”</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-11.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78638\" srcset=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-11.png 1152w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-11.png 229w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-11.png 783w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-11.png 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1152px) 100vw, 1152px\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>The portrait Saetia made for McAllister of her son Eddie, who died in 2024, with her granddaughter</em></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Her reaction made a deep impression on her teenage charge, inspiring him to launch his nonprofit, <a href=\"https://eternalcanvas.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">The Eternal Canvas Foundation</a>, which gifts oil paintings of late loved ones to grieving family members. “That moment became kinda like my mission,” said Saetia, now 17. </p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">He began by respectfully approaching mourners at the cemetery where his mom is buried, asking if they’d be interested in a free portrait of their loved one. He paid for supplies — paints, brushes, canvases — with the money he made helping out his dad and brother sharpen knives at a farmers’ market on weekends. Eventually, he started using an internet platform to commission artists across the world, many of whom have experienced loss themselves. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-instagram wp-block-embed-instagram\">\n<blockquote class=\"instagram-media\" data-instgrm-captioned data-instgrm-permalink=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/DZ2wvSMiQ9F/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\" data-instgrm-version=\"14\"></blockquote></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">About a year ago, he gathered the funds to register the foundation for tax-exempt status under section 501(c)(3), and currently, Eternal Canvas has about 400 active requests. Saetia himself completes as many portraits as he can, a process he admitted can sometimes be emotional. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">“Grief is something that’s so personal, but it’s universal as well. It’s like everyone experiences it differently, and whenever I’m painting someone else’s lost loved one, I have to remember that this was someone’s life, you know?” he shared. “They had their own world, they had their own story, in a sense. It’s really surreal.” </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-instagram wp-block-embed-instagram\">\n<blockquote class=\"instagram-media\" data-instgrm-captioned data-instgrm-permalink=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/DV6jAAJj22v/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\" data-instgrm-version=\"14\"></blockquote></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">One story that sticks with him involves a portrait he painted of a woman from Samoa. She’d traveled to the U.S. to care for her adult daughter who was battling cancer, but then developed cancer herself. Not wanting to cause her daughter any stress, she kept her diagnosis to herself until her last month. “Her family just commended her for being so strong and keeping that within,” Saetia recounted. </p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The rising senior, who’s also a school wrestler, said that the portraits reconnected him to art — a pastime he’d enjoyed as a young child but had prioritized less as his interest in sports grew. “I started to fall back in love with art when I started doing Eternal Canvas. So it was a really full-circle moment when I saw what the power of art could do.”</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">He’s now working on another portrait for McAllister, this time of her husband and sons. “There’s so many other things that he could be doing,” she said, adding, “And you know it’s coming from his heart. He’s putting all of himself into it. It’s just a great thing.”</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-54-731x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78600\" srcset=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-54-731x1024.jpg 731w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-54-214x300.jpg 214w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-54-768x1075.jpg 768w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-54-1097x1536.jpg 1097w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-54.jpg 1100w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 731px) 100vw, 731px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Screenshot</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>A portrait by Saetia of himself and his late mother, who died when he was 6</em> </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Those interested in requesting a portrait can do so on The Eternal Canvas Foundation website. You can also <a href=\"https://eternalcanvas.org/donate/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">make one-time or recurring donations</a> to help Saetia and his team of artists continue creating paintings.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">“I think that I’m giving them almost, like, a doorway into this person’s life,” said Saetia of the people who receive the artwork. “This isn’t just a portrait. It is kind of <em>somebody</em>, you know? Somebody that had a presence on Earth and someone that, for the family, continues to live on in their own hearts.”</p>\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t</div>\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_7367-2-1-1.jpg","t":"2026-09-02","p":"","n":0},"https://nicenews.com/science/how-complex-mental-maps-spatial-reasoning-protect-brain/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"entry-content clear\" ast-blocks-layout=\"true\" itemprop=\"text\">\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>This article was written by <a href=\"https://theconversation.com/profiles/hatim-sharif-2426792\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Hatim Sharif</a>, a professor of civil and environmental engineering at The University of Texas at San Antonio, for </em><a href=\"https://theconversation.com/us\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><em>The Conversation</em></a><em> — a nonprofit news organization dedicated to sharing the knowledge of researchers and scientists, under a </em><a href=\"https://theconversation.com/us/who-we-are\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><em>Creative Commons license</em></a><em>. Read the original article <a href=\"https://theconversation.com/taxi-drivers-rarely-die-of-alzheimers-how-complex-mental-maps-and-spatial-reasoning-protect-your-brain-286650\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">here</a>.</em></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Taxi and ambulance drivers are less likely than workers in almost any other job to <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj-2024-082194\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">die of Alzheimer’s disease</a>. That was the surprising result of a 2024 study examining the death certificates of nearly 9 million people in the U.S.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">These findings stopped me in my tracks because those two jobs rely on the same thing as my own work: maps.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">I have spent more than two decades staring at maps. Not paper maps on a wall, but digital ones with multiple layers: flood boundaries draped over census blocks, car crash hot spots plotted against road geometry, and satellite readings of rainfall stitched across river basins. Much of my work as a <a href=\"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=ZJTicOQAAAAJ&amp;hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">civil and environmental engineer</a> is done through <a href=\"https://theconversation.com/mapping-cemeteries-for-class-how-students-used-phones-and-drones-to-help-a-city-count-its-headstones-273154\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">GIS — that is, geographic information systems</a>. Engineers like me hold several spatial relationships in their minds at once, reasoning about where things sit relative to one another across scales ranging from a city block to a whole watershed.</p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">I always assumed that spatial reasoning across map layers was purely professional. But that study on taxi and ambulance drivers made me wonder whether all that mental work might be doing something good to the brain.</p>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-taxi-driver-brains\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Taxi Driver Brains</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Of the 9 million death certificates from January 2020 to December 2022 that researchers examined, taxi and ambulance drivers had the <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj-2024-082194\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">lowest risk of dying from Alzheimer’s disease</a> out of 443 occupations. After adjusting for age, sex, race, ethnicity, and education, roughly 1 in 100 taxi and ambulance drivers died of Alzheimer’s, compared with 1 in 60 people overall.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This pattern did not extend to other driving jobs. The researchers concluded that the key to reducing the risk of Alzheimer’s was not driving itself but continuous real-time navigation: the constant work of locating yourself in space, tracking a destination, and updating a <a href=\"https://theconversation.com/how-does-your-brain-decide-between-the-road-not-taken-or-the-same-old-route-resolving-conflicting-memories-is-key-to-navigation-279435\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">mental map</a> as conditions change. Drivers whose jobs relied on <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj-2024-082194\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">fixed or predetermined routes</a>, like bus drivers and aircraft pilots, didn’t seem to experience a similar advantage.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Researchers believe the association between navigation-heavy work and lower Alzheimer’s risk centers on the hippocampus, a part of the brain that governs memory and spatial navigation. It’s one of the first brain regions that Alzheimer’s damages: <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41582-018-0031-x\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Problems with spatial navigation and orientation</a> are among the earliest signs of the disease, sometimes surfacing before obvious memory loss.</p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In one landmark 2000 study, neuroscientists compared the brains of licensed London taxi drivers with those of people who did not drive cabs. Their findings provided the first evidence via structural imaging that regions of the <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.070039597\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">adult brain can measurably change</a> under sustained navigational demand. To earn a license, London cabbies must memorize more than 25,000 streets within a 6-mile radius of Charing Cross, a challenge known as “<a href=\"https://tfl.gov.uk/info-for/taxis-and-private-hire/licensing/learn-the-knowledge-of-london\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">The Knowledge</a>” that takes three to four years.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Can you memorize 25,000 streets and how to navigate them?</em></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The researchers found that London taxi drivers had measurably more gray matter in the posterior hippocampus, a brain area tied to storing large-scale spatial maps. That volume <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.070039597\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">tracked with experience</a>: The longer someone had driven, the larger that part of the brain. The change was built through practice, not inherited. While people who are good at navigation might gravitate to this kind of job, the job itself does have an impact on the brain.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Together, these two studies make a coherent case: Work that intensively exercises the hippocampus may reshape it, and that reshaping may protect against one of the most feared diseases of aging.</p>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-where-map-specialists-fit-in\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Where Map Specialists Fit in</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cartographers, urban planners, and geospatial analysts spend their working days in <a href=\"https://www.aag.org/jobs-careers/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">sustained spatial reasoning</a>. A geographic information system specialist might use a computer to overlap population data on flood exposure maps to find who is at risk, or read satellite imagery to map land cover after a wildfire. Researchers juggle several layers of data, coordinate systems and scales at once.</p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Does spatial reasoning through a screen engage the hippocampus the way moving through a real city does?</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">While a taxi driver navigates from inside the scene at street level, GIS researchers picture space from above as a map — what cognitive scientists call <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tics.2006.10.005\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">allocentric reasoning</a>. But these two perspectives overlap in the brain: The hippocampus also builds maps from outside viewpoints, not just from a navigator’s own position.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Research on cognitive maps points toward the same conclusion as the study on taxi drivers. In 2023, researchers ran a machine learning model on more than 22,500 people in a national dataset and were able to predict which ZIP codes had higher rates of Alzheimer’s with 84% accuracy based on how complex the environment was. Those <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.14283/jpad.2023.18\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">living in spatially complex surroundings</a> — the kind that force active map building, such as dense street networks with numerous intersections, diverse points of interest and landmarks, and multiple path options — were less likely to develop Alzheimer’s.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/file-20260805-50-1x5k83-1024x682.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78556\" srcset=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/file-20260805-50-1x5k83-1024x682.jpg 1024w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/file-20260805-50-1x5k83-300x200.jpg 300w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/file-20260805-50-1x5k83-768x512.jpg 768w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/file-20260805-50-1x5k83-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/file-20260805-50-1x5k83.jpg 1907w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">fhm—Moment/Getty Images</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Living in spatially complex places challenges your brain.</em></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A follow-up study tied geospatial complexity in one’s environment to greater volume in the brain’s spatial navigation regions. The researchers hypothesized that routinely building cognitive maps <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1002/dad2.12551\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">exercises the very circuitry</a> that Alzheimer’s attacks first. Repeatedly engaging the cognitive systems involved in spatial navigation could help delay symptoms of disease.</p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">However, these two studies focus on where people live, not the work people do. Whether spatial reasoning through a screen exercises the same circuitry as real-life city navigation remains untested.</p>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-protecting-your-brain\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Protecting Your Brain</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The implications of whether sustained spatial reasoning protects the brain reach beyond mapmakers and cab drivers. Studies have repeatedly found a link between mentally complex occupations and <a href=\"https://www.alz.org/getmedia/ba1ae239-1461-44ec-bc20-d297db776739/ph-bold-center-science-summary-education.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">delayed cognitive decline and lower dementia risk</a>, even after accounting for education.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Research on <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/S1474-4422(12)70191-6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">cognitive reserve</a> — the brain’s capacity to continue functioning despite disease — can help explain why two people with a similar disease burden can show markedly different levels of cognitive impairment. If demanding spatial thinking protects the brain, then how societies design schooling, professional training, and retirement all become questions of brain health.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Spatial reasoning <a href=\"https://dx.doi.org/10.1037/a0028446\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">can be trained</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.aag.org/guide-to-geography-programs-and-opportunities/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">training opportunities</a> are already widespread. GIS and remote sensing instruction are available through geography, engineering, public health, and environmental science programs worldwide.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If sustained engagement with spatial reasoning can help the brain strengthen the circuitry that Alzheimer’s attacks first, its value reaches well beyond the technical skills it builds.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">RELATED: <a href=\"https://nicenews.com/health-and-wellness/expert-tips-reduce-alzheimers-risk/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">40% of Alzheimer’s Cases Are Preventable — How You Can Reduce Your Risk, According to an Expert</a></p>\t\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://counter.theconversation.com/content/286650/count.gif\" alt=\"The Conversation\"></figure>\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t</div>\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/file-20260805-60-8x6hvk.jpg","t":"2026-09-02","p":"","n":0},"https://nicenews.com/environment/what-do-dog-cat-choking-vet/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"entry-content clear\" ast-blocks-layout=\"true\" itemprop=\"text\">\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">At least a few times a month, I Google, ‚ÄúCan dogs eat … ‚Äù followed by whichever of my snacks my Chihuahua mix is eyeing woefully (most recently it was mango, and <a href=\"https://www.purina.com/articles/dog/feeding/can-dogs-eat/mango\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">the answer is yes</a>, in moderation). </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">All loving pet parents want their animal companions to be happy and healthy, and a lot of that comes down to what goes into their mouths ‚Äî so I was taken aback when I realized one day that I had no clue what I‚Äôd do if my pup started choking. Perform the Heimlich? Administer a few slaps to the back? Start running around in circles in complete and utter panic?</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-tiktok wp-block-embed-tiktok\">\n<blockquote class=\"tiktok-embed\" cite=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@20points4gryffindor/video/7637247700546751758\" data-video-id=\"7637247700546751758\" data-embed-from=\"oembed\">  </blockquote> \n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">To avoid the third option ever becoming reality, I reached out to veterinarian Jinni Sinnott-Stutzman, senior director of clinical affairs for <a href=\"https://vcahospitals.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">VCA Animal Hospitals</a>. She walked me through how to help prevent dogs and cats from choking, as well as what to do if it does happen. Most importantly, though, she reassured me about the rarity of the scenario. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">‚ÄúChoking is a scary thing to think about, but I want pet owners to know it’s rare. Pets, like people, are typically protective of their throats,‚Äù Sinnott-Stutzman said, adding that as long as we follow the preventative measures outlined below, ‚Äúit‚Äôs very likely a person owning multiple pets in their lifetime will never encounter choking.‚Äù</p>\t\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-how-can-we-help-prevent-pets-from-choking\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How Can We Help Prevent Pets From Choking?</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1795133707-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78584\" srcset=\"https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1795133707-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1795133707-300x200.jpg 300w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1795133707-768x512.jpg 768w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1795133707-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1795133707-2048x1365.jpg 2048w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Chalabala‚ÄîiStock/Getty Images Plus</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-avoid-choking-size-objects\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Avoid ‚ÄúChoking Size‚Äù Objects</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">One of the most effective ways to prevent your dog or cat from choking is to prevent their access to food and toys that are ‚Äúchoking size.‚Äù Exact measurements will vary based on the breed and individual, but Sinnott-Stutzman explained that choking size is generally the diameter of the <a href=\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/body/21869-pharynx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">pharynx</a> (the back of the throat). </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">‚ÄúFor a cat or small dog, this is about the size of a plump cherry. For a medium dog, it’s the size of a golf ball, and for your larger dogs, it‚Äôs the size of a tennis ball,‚Äù she said. ‚ÄúSpeaking of tennis balls, that is the most common choke I’ve seen. Typically, large dogs try to catch a ball and miss the timing and get it stuck in the back of their throat. There are <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V92nhEmKbvs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">great YouTube videos on the exact technique</a> to use to get it out, but it’s a little technical. That said, it can save a life, so I always tell every ER vet to learn it.‚Äù</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Thankfully, tennis balls made specifically for dogs come in various sizes, so if your big pup likes to play fetch, be sure to <a href=\"https://www.chewy.com/kong-squeakair-ball-dog-toy/dp/105550\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">purchase balls on the larger side </a>(rather than standard human tennis balls). </p>\t\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1372204500-1024x764.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78578\" srcset=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1372204500-1024x764.jpg 1024w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1372204500-300x224.jpg 300w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1372204500-768x573.jpg 768w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1372204500-1536x1145.jpg 1536w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1372204500-2048x1527.jpg 2048w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">nycshooter‚ÄîE+/Getty Images</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For small dogs, it‚Äôs best to opt for the biggest size ball they can actually carry ‚Äî not the teeny-weeny ones, as cute as they may be. </p>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-supervise-them\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Supervise Them</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Be sure to never leave your dog unattended with bones, rawhides, balls, and toys that have smaller elements inside (like squeakers), or anything else they can gnaw down or tear apart into choking-size chunks. By supervising them during play, meal, and snack times, you can remove small bits as your pet makes progress on his treat or toy.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sinnott-Stutzman said that cats don‚Äôt often choke ‚Äî but ‚Äúwhen they do, it’s usually on something linear that they are playing with and then start to swallow, so you can usually pull the string, plastic bag handle, or whatever is still sticking out of the mouth to save them.‚Äù  </p>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-give-food-in-small-bites\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Give Food in Small Bites</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">That said, Sinnott-Stutzman has seen very hungry rescue kittens choke on wet food, so be sure to give them small bites for their first meals ‚Äúas they may inhale an entire mouthful and try to swallow it,‚Äù she noted. ‚ÄúOnce they have had a few good meals and are on a positive calorie balance, they can be fed normally.‚Äù</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1158693662-1024x701.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78579\" srcset=\"https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1158693662-1024x701.jpg 1024w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1158693662-300x205.jpg 300w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1158693662-768x526.jpg 768w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1158693662-1536x1051.jpg 1536w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1158693662-2048x1402.jpg 2048w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Lisa5201‚ÄîE+/Getty Images</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The same sentiment can be applied to any ravenous dog or cat (and let‚Äôs be honest, even the most well-fed pets often act as though they haven‚Äôt eaten in days). If you give your dog or cat fresh or canned food, ensure it‚Äôs broken up into bite-size pieces. </p>\t\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-how-can-you-tell-if-a-dog-or-cat-is-choking\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How Can You Tell if a Dog or Cat Is Choking?</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Per Sinnott-Stutzman, there are two kinds of choking. ‚ÄúThere’s discomfort from having something lodged in the back of [the] throat but air is moving through, and there‚Äôs complete obstruction of air movement,‚Äù she explained, noting that the first type ‚Äúis scary to watch, because your pet is gagging, pawing at their mouth, and making really raspy breathing noises. The second kind is scary, period, end of sentence.‚Äù</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The main difference between the two is whether or not the pet is making sounds. If your pet is crying, whimpering, or making rasping sounds while breathing, their airway likely isn’t <em>completely </em>obstructed, but they still need immediate attention. In this instance, you should get them to the nearest open veterinary clinic as soon as possible. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If they aren‚Äôt making any noise ‚Äî other than maybe a soft gagging sound ‚Äî the airway may indeed be completely obstructed. In that case, jump into action using the instructions below. </p>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-steps-to-take-if-your-dog-or-cat-is-choking\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Steps to Take if Your Dog or Cat Is Choking</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>1.</strong> Look in your pet‚Äôs mouth and see if there‚Äôs a visible object. If there is, try to grasp it with your fingers and sweep it forward and out ‚Äî but be extremely careful to avoid pushing it further down the airway.<strong> </strong>Sinnott-Stutzman recommends having another person hold open the animal‚Äôs jaws if possible, as even a loving pet may bite when panicked. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>2.</strong> If you can see the object but can‚Äôt get it out with your hands, you can carefully attempt to pull it toward you using the flat side of a spoon with a long handle. Again, be sure not to chase the item further down the throat, and don‚Äôt let go of the spoon once it’s in the animal‚Äôs mouth. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>3.</strong> If you can’t see or remove the object manually, lift your dog or cat up by their back legs, keeping their front legs on the ground to avoid straining the back, and gently shake them. You want to use gravity to move the object out of the mouth. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>4. </strong>If the object doesn‚Äôt come out, try gently swinging your dog or cat back and forth (the key word here is gently) as you hold them from their hind legs. You can also administer five sharp blows to the animal‚Äôs back between their shoulder blades. Use less force for smaller dogs and cats to avoid hurting them. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>5. </strong>If your dog is still choking, <a href=\"https://www.redcross.org/take-a-class/resources/learn-pet-first-aid/dog/choking\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">you can try the Heimlich maneuver</a>. Stand behind or lift the dog with its spine against your chest, then wrap your arms around and under its ribs. Make a fist with one hand, place your other hand over your fist, and give five rapid abdominal thrusts in an inward and upward motion, varying the force based on the size of your pup.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sinnott-Stutzman said she‚Äôs more comfortable recommending the Heimlich for dogs than for cats due to their delicate ribs, but if <a href=\"https://www.redcross.org/take-a-class/resources/learn-pet-first-aid/cat/choking?srsltid=AfmBOop53MrcgkG8ptv-qpukY5aPY_omSHwa4OPvwQUCFv2cqTgbVP7t\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">you do use the technique</a> on felines, use gentler thrusts, and you probably don‚Äôt need to use your entire fist.</p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>6.</strong> Lastly, if the item is a ball or other round object, Sinnott-Stutzman advocates ‚Äúplaying vet‚Äù by using the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/53kRQTtsWno\">external extraction technique</a>, or XXT.  </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">‚ÄúIt’s not for the faint of heart, and again, if your pet is moving air (making noises beyond soft gagging sounds), go to the vet,‚Äù she said. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-9-16 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">‚ÄúBut if they are not, you don’t have a lot of time, so it’s better to try than nothing. Just don’t spend long trying if you’re unsuccessful after one or two tries ‚Äî use the time to get to the vet.‚Äù </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t</div>\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1365277062-scaled.jpg","t":"2026-09-02","p":"","n":0},"https://nicenews.com/culture/regrets-people-over-50-traveling/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"entry-content clear\" ast-blocks-layout=\"true\" itemprop=\"text\">\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>This article was originally written by Ruby Copp for SWNS — the U.K.’s largest independent news agency, providing globally relevant original, verified, and engaging content to the world’s leading media outlets.</em><br></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The older we get the more <a href=\"https://www.psychologytoday.com/us/blog/out-of-the-darkness/202409/why-does-time-seem-to-speed-up-as-we-get-older\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">we feel time speeding up</a> — and that’s when those “I wish I would have” thoughts begin to creep in at an unwelcome pace. According to a recent survey, the biggest regret for people over 50 wasn’t related to saving money or even keeping in touch with old friends: It was simply not having traveled more. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Commissioned by Icelandair (in headlines recently for <a href=\"https://www.icelandair.com/flights/campaign/really-bad-photographer/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">seeking the world’s worst photographer</a> to win a trip to the country), the poll recruited 2,000 people to share where they wished they’d visited but never had. The three locations that came out on top? New Zealand, Japan, and Australia. Canada, the Maldives, and Iceland are also in the top 10 destinations participants wanted to travel to.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Among the other experiences participants over 50 would like to have prioritized more were taking spontaneous trips without overthinking it (21%), going to bucket list destinations (17%), and saying “yes” to adventures rather than focusing on work (14%). </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-2204281236-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78495\" srcset=\"https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-2204281236-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-2204281236-300x200.jpg 300w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-2204281236-768x512.jpg 768w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-2204281236-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-2204281236-2048x1365.jpg 2048w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Elena Zolotova—iStock Editorial/Getty Images Plus</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">And it’s not just the older generations who have travel pangs — 42% of Gen Zers and 47% of millennials additionally reported wishing they’d been able to travel more than they have so far. </p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It also emerged 71% of all adults polled are adamant it is never too late to make up for lost time. Many believe seeing new places (37%) or experiencing natural phenomena (18%) will still positively impact their lives. For Gen Zers and millennials, seeing the northern lights topped their lists of the most-coveted once-in-a-lifetime experiences. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">“Travel has never been more accessible, but our research shows once-in-a-lifetime experiences still sit firmly on people’s bucket lists and too many never get ticked off, leaving them with regrets about the things they didn’t do,” a spokesperson for Icelandair said in a statement. “We wanted to turn that idea on its head and encourage people to stop putting unforgettable experiences off and go live them.”</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-663874486-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78494\" srcset=\"https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-663874486-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-663874486-300x200.jpg 300w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-663874486-768x512.jpg 768w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-663874486-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-663874486-2048x1365.jpg 2048w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">LeoPatrizi—E+/Getty Images</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Iceland</em></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The airline’s exciting (albeit tongue-in-cheek) idea for helping people make that happen? Launching a contest to send someone on a trip to see the next total solar eclipse that will be visible from Iceland — 170 years from now. “If you’re going to think big, why not think really big?” the spokesperson said. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They added: “With many often waiting for the right time, it’s a reminder some experiences are worth making happen — whether that’s this year, next year, or something you pass down for generations to come because you never know what might be on the bucket list of your future great-great-grandchildren, or give them the chance to say, ‘I was there.’” The contest also includes a trip to Iceland next month, so <a href=\"https://icelandair-ehf.campaign.playable.com/solar-eclipse\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">enter soon</a> if you’re interested.</p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For all adults, a lack of financial security was the top barrier to achieving their travel goals (44%), followed by family responsibilities (24%) and other priorities getting in the way (22%). And 19% admitted they are always waiting for the “right time” — a figure that rose 31% for Gen Z.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The study, carried out via OnePoll, found the average adult believes they’ll experience five truly once-in-a-lifetime moments. But many are optimistic this will increase for their grandchildren’s generation, with 47% hopeful the younger crowd will be able to make the most of life and 38% wanting them to enjoy the natural world more.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">“Travel gives us a great opportunity for lifetime experiences,” the spokesperson for Icelandair added. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">See how your travel wishlist and regrets compare to the poll results: </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Top Bucket List Destinations for People Over 50</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">1. New Zealand</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">2. Japan</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">3. Australia</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">4. Canada</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">5. Maldives</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">6. Iceland</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">7. Norway</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">8. Italy</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">9. Egypt</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">10. Vietnam</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Top Things People Over 50 Wish They’d Experienced</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">1. Traveled more</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">2. Saved more money</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">3. Not lost touch with friends</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">4. Not worried too much about what others think</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">5. Make the most of life</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">6. Looked after their health</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">7. Made the most of their youth</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">8. Spent enough time with loved ones before they passed away</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">9. Learned a second language</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">10. Exercised more</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">11. Learned to play an instrument</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">12. Said how they really felt more often</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">13. Spent enough time with family</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">14. Taken spontaneous trips without overthinking it</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">15. Gained more qualifications</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">16. Not stayed in an unhappy job for too long</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">17. Been more spontaneous generally</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">18. Travelled to bucket list destinations</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">19. Not worked too much</p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">20. Taken more risks</p>\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t</div>\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1415070790-1-scaled.jpg","t":"2026-09-01","p":"","n":0},"https://workspaces.beehiiv.com/p/240-jack-zerby":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"_10pdwo80 dream-post-content-doc\"><div class=\"_1gqvddm0\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://www.jackzerby.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Jack Zerby</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> is currently the Head of Design at </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"http://gumroad.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Gumroad</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> and Founder of </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"http://dogma.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Dogma</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"http://designfordecks.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Design For Decks</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"http://biddyhq.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Biddy</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"http://getdohq.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">DOHQ</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://Flavors.me\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Flavors.me</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, and </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/what-is-goodsie-2011-5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Goodsie</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">. </span><br><br><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">He has worked for companies like </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://vimeo.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Vimeo</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://pentagram.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Pentagram</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://frogdesign.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Frog</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://rga.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">R/GA</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> and consulted for companies like </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://teachable.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Teachable</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://americanexpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Amex</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, and </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://staked.us/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Staked</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">.</span></p></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What gear is included in your workspace?</span></h2></p><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What is your favorite item in your workspace?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">My desk is definitely my fave. It’s got an old classic feel with the benefits of a modern standing desk.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">How do you spark creativity?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Lo-Fi beats station on Spotify and phone on silent. Love sites like siteinspire.com, but will also go to Barnes and Noble and buy a bunch of beautiful magazines in any category.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">How do you manage work-life balance?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">I run everything through Notion and create tickets for all tasks for that week along with goals for each quarter. I stop work at 5:30 no matter what, eat dinner and hang with the fam till bedtime. No work on weekends helps clear my mind and prevent burnout.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What do you think is the main benefit of remote work?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">No distractions, no commuting and ability to structure my day around tasks to be completed, not the amount of hours at my desk.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></body></html>","i":"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,quality=80,width=1200,onerror=redirect/uploads/asset/file/83ffefc4-12e8-4eba-83aa-2833cea00251/Jack_Zerby_thumbnail.png?t=1781142493","t":"2026-09-02","p":"","n":0},"https://blog.zhheo.com/p/c0jzc71f.html":{"c":"<p>智谱昨天活动送2000积分，正好用来判断牛来模型 GLM-5.3-Flash 的耐用程度，看看值不值得买。当然，我们的判断基准线就是opencode go 10刀（大概接近70人民币）来计算。低于这个就不适合买，高于这个就可以买。</p>\n<p>GLM-5.3-Flash 我在使用zcode进行编程开发的时候，我发现Cache 命中率奇低，只有8开头。</p>\n<p>我们先比较纯数值。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"计划\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/5487020260828072600.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<p>opencode go只给了15刀额度（只代表这个模型只能用15刀，超出部分可以用其他模型）</p>\n<p>那我们就拼一下，15刀的GLM-5.3-Flash+15刀的DeepSeek V4 Flash Vision Exp (Off-Peak)+30刀的DeepSeek V4 Flash (Off-Peak)实现拼60刀。</p>\n<p>按照95%缓存来算，opencode go 大致为24～26 亿 token/月。（不过我目前主力在用 Muse Spark 1.2 Contributor 作为vibecoding首选模型，可以用75～80 亿 token/月）。</p>\n<p>智谱的话lite套餐一个月118元，周10000积分，月40000积分。先当于5小时限额的20倍。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"限额\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/3787420260828075733.jpeg!blogimg\"/></p>\n<p>用了大概43分钟跑满了限额（单线程，zcode编程），如果多线程跑会更快。用了大概2千万token。算下来的话目测pro套餐勉强够用。max套餐绰绰有余。</p>\n<p>用量就算出来了，lite套餐 4.3亿token左右。pro 25亿token左右，max 60亿token左右。</p>\n<p>所以说opencode相当于70元买了智谱538一个月的pro套餐了。气笑了。看来国内tokenplan是一个都用不了，国人模型专坑国人诚不欺我。</p>\n<p>目前如果想买到经济实惠的token，tokenplan的主要选择就是 gpt、opencode、commandcode这三种了。</p>\n<p><strong>啥时候能再有一个deepseek涨价之前用opencode的那种实力和价格（相当于之前deepseek v4 flash api 价格除以12）的模型啊。。。</strong></p>\n<p>目前我还在用Muse Spark 1.2 Contributor 勉强度日，还不知道我opencode用完该何去何从了。</p>\n<p>另外：</p>\n<p>用zcode今天可以领3亿token。。。（是时候领鸡蛋了，需要更新到最新版本，点击左下角有个活动卡片，今晚8点开始可用）</p>\n<p><img alt=\"领鸡蛋\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/3822020260828084853.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"活动说明\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/3094020260828085052.jpg!blogimg\"/></p>\n","i":"","t":"2026-09-02","p":"","n":0},"https://blog.zhheo.com/p/mrlh0a7v.html":{"c":"<p>家里跑了好几个服务，Home Assistant、SearXNG、Alist、Emby，还有签到之类的杂七杂八。每个服务一个端口，手机上记端口记到崩溃。</p>\n<p>以前我用 HeoSafe 拦截方案做访问控制，检测到流量直接弹身份认证。能用，但本质上还是请求到了之后再拦，配置维护比较重，算不上好的解决方式。</p>\n<p>后来想通了，干脆把链路整清楚：<strong>ZeroTier 组网 + DNS 域名解析 + iStore Nginx 反代 + certd 证书管理</strong>，一套走通。</p>\n<h2 id=\"硬件和系统\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#硬件和系统\" title=\"硬件和系统\"></a>硬件和系统</h2><p>R5S 软路由刷的 iStoreOS，基于 OpenWrt。Nginx 通过 iStore 应用商店直接装，不是 Docker。这个很重要，因为 iStore 装的 Nginx 有自己一套 UCI 配置，和传统手动装的不一样。</p>\n<p>装完之后 Nginx 自动接管 <code>80/443</code>，uHTTPd 原来的 LuCI 也被接管了，不用额外折腾。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"nginx安装\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/6157220260828054652.jpg!blogimg\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"ZeroTier-组网\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#ZeroTier-组网\" title=\"ZeroTier 组网\"></a>ZeroTier 组网</h2><p>ZeroTier 解决的是跨网络访问问题。装完客户端加入同一个网络，设备之间就像在同一个局域网里。</p>\n<p>R5S 上 ZeroTier 分配的内网 IP 是 <code>10.225.17.77</code>。手机、电脑、iPad 加入同一个网络后都能直接访问这个 IP。</p>\n<p>但 IP 记不住，所以需要 DNS。</p>\n<h2 id=\"DNS-解析\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#DNS-解析\" title=\"DNS 解析\"></a>DNS 解析</h2><p>域名 <code>zhheo.com</code> 托管在腾讯云 DNSPod，直接在 DNSPod 加 A 记录：</p>\n<figure class=\"highlight text\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/><span class=\"line\">2</span><br/><span class=\"line\">3</span><br/><span class=\"line\">4</span><br/><span class=\"line\">5</span><br/><span class=\"line\">6</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\">s.zhheo.com        → 10.225.17.77</span><br/><span class=\"line\">heohass.zhheo.com  → 10.225.17.77</span><br/><span class=\"line\">heodisk.zhheo.com  → 10.225.17.77</span><br/><span class=\"line\">emby.zhheo.com     → 10.225.17.77</span><br/><span class=\"line\">qiandao.zhheo.com  → 10.225.17.77</span><br/><span class=\"line\">certd.zhheo.com    → 10.225.17.77</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<p>这里的 IP 是 ZeroTier 内网 IP，不是公网 IP。所以这些域名只有加入 ZeroTier 网络的设备才能访问，公网打不通。这反而是个安全优势。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Nginx-反向代理\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#Nginx-反向代理\" title=\"Nginx 反向代理\"></a>Nginx 反向代理</h2><p>Nginx 装好之后，配一个反代配置文件就行。我放在 <code>/etc/nginx/conf.d/zhheo-services.conf</code>，iStore 的 Nginx 会自动加载这个目录下的 <code>.conf</code> 文件。</p>\n<p>每个域名对应一个后端端口：</p>\n<figure class=\"highlight text\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/><span class=\"line\">2</span><br/><span class=\"line\">3</span><br/><span class=\"line\">4</span><br/><span class=\"line\">5</span><br/><span class=\"line\">6</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\">s.zhheo.com        → 127.0.0.1:19080   # SearXNG</span><br/><span class=\"line\">heohass.zhheo.com  → 127.0.0.1:8123    # Home Assistant</span><br/><span class=\"line\">heodisk.zhheo.com  → 127.0.0.1:5244    # Alist</span><br/><span class=\"line\">emby.zhheo.com     → 127.0.0.1:18080   # Emby</span><br/><span class=\"line\">qiandao.zhheo.com  → 127.0.0.1:8923    # 签到</span><br/><span class=\"line\">certd.zhheo.com    → 127.0.0.1:12281   # certd</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<p>配置模板大概是这样：</p>\n<figure class=\"highlight nginx\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/><span class=\"line\">2</span><br/><span class=\"line\">3</span><br/><span class=\"line\">4</span><br/><span class=\"line\">5</span><br/><span class=\"line\">6</span><br/><span class=\"line\">7</span><br/><span class=\"line\">8</span><br/><span class=\"line\">9</span><br/><span class=\"line\">10</span><br/><span class=\"line\">11</span><br/><span class=\"line\">12</span><br/><span class=\"line\">13</span><br/><span class=\"line\">14</span><br/><span class=\"line\">15</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"section\">server</span> {</span><br/><span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"attribute\">listen</span> <span class=\"number\">443</span> ssl;</span><br/><span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"attribute\">server_name</span> heohass.zhheo.com;</span><br/><span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"attribute\">ssl_certificate</span> /etc/nginx/conf.d/wildcard.zhheo.com.crt;</span><br/><span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"attribute\">ssl_certificate_key</span> /etc/nginx/conf.d/wildcard.zhheo.com.key;</span><br/><span class=\"line\"></span><br/><span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"section\">location</span> / {</span><br/><span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"attribute\">proxy_pass</span> http://127.0.0.1:8123;</span><br/><span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"attribute\">proxy_set_header</span> Host <span class=\"variable\">$host</span>;</span><br/><span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"attribute\">proxy_http_version</span> <span class=\"number\">1</span>.<span class=\"number\">1</span>;</span><br/><span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"attribute\">proxy_set_header</span> Upgrade <span class=\"variable\">$http_upgrade</span>;</span><br/><span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"attribute\">proxy_set_header</span> Connection <span class=\"string\">\"upgrade\"</span>;</span><br/><span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"attribute\">proxy_read_timeout</span> <span class=\"number\">3600s</span>;</span><br/><span class=\"line\">    }</span><br/><span class=\"line\">}</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<p>Home Assistant 需要 WebSocket 支持，所以加了 <code>Upgrade</code> 和 <code>Connection</code> 头。其他服务一般不需要，但加上也没坏处。</p>\n<p>改完配置后：</p>\n<figure class=\"highlight sh\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\">nginx -t -c /etc/nginx/uci.conf &amp;&amp; nginx -s reload -c /etc/nginx/uci.conf</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<p>iStore 的 Nginx 必须用 <code>-c /etc/nginx/uci.conf</code>，直接 <code>nginx -t</code> 会报找不到文件。</p>\n<h2 id=\"certd-证书管理\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#certd-证书管理\" title=\"certd 证书管理\"></a>certd 证书管理</h2><p>裸 HTTP 能用，但手机浏览器会弹不安全提示。所以用 certd 管理通配符证书。</p>\n<p>certd 也是 Docker 部署在 R5S 上的，自动申请和续期证书。部署方式选的是「主机-部署证书到 SSH 主机」，直接把证书文件写到 R5S 宿主机：</p>\n<p><img alt=\"添加步骤\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/9982320260828054924.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<figure class=\"highlight text\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/><span class=\"line\">2</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\">/etc/nginx/conf.d/wildcard.zhheo.com.crt</span><br/><span class=\"line\">/etc/nginx/conf.d/wildcard.zhheo.com.key</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<p>部署完成后 Nginx 不会自动读取新证书，必须手动 reload：</p>\n<figure class=\"highlight sh\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\">nginx -t -c /etc/nginx/uci.conf &amp;&amp; nginx -s reload -c /etc/nginx/uci.conf</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<p>这里踩了个坑：iStore 的 Nginx UCI 配置里有个选项叫 <code>uci_manage_ssl</code>，默认值是 <code>self-signed</code>。不关掉它，Nginx reload 时会自动生成自签名证书，覆盖掉你刚部署的通配符证书。解决方法：</p>\n<figure class=\"highlight sh\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/><span class=\"line\">2</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\">uci delete nginx._lan.uci_manage_ssl</span><br/><span class=\"line\">uci commit nginx</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<p>删掉这个选项之后，Nginx 就不会自动搞证书了。</p>\n<p>另外私钥权限设成 <code>600</code>：</p>\n<figure class=\"highlight sh\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"built_in\">chmod</span> 600 /etc/nginx/conf.d/wildcard.zhheo.com.key</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<h2 id=\"完整链路\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#完整链路\" title=\"完整链路\"></a>完整链路</h2><figure class=\"highlight text\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/><span class=\"line\">2</span><br/><span class=\"line\">3</span><br/><span class=\"line\">4</span><br/><span class=\"line\">5</span><br/><span class=\"line\">6</span><br/><span class=\"line\">7</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\">手机/电脑/iPad</span><br/><span class=\"line\">  ↓ ZeroTier 组网</span><br/><span class=\"line\">R5S 软路由（10.225.17.77）</span><br/><span class=\"line\">  ↓ DNS 域名解析</span><br/><span class=\"line\">Nginx 反向代理（80/443）</span><br/><span class=\"line\">  ↓ 按域名分发</span><br/><span class=\"line\">各服务后端端口</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<p>体验上就是：加入 ZeroTier 网络后，手机浏览器直接输入 <code>https://heohass.zhheo.com</code>，无警告、无拦截，直接到 Home Assistant。</p>\n<p>比之前 HeoSafe 的方案清爽多了。</p>\n<h2 id=\"踩坑记录\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#踩坑记录\" title=\"踩坑记录\"></a>踩坑记录</h2><ol>\n<li><strong>iStore Nginx 的 <code>nginx -t</code> 要加 <code>-c /etc/nginx/uci.conf</code></strong>，否则直接报错。</li>\n<li><strong><code>uci_manage_ssl='self-signed'</code> 会覆盖证书文件</strong>，部署正式证书前必须删掉。</li>\n<li><strong>Nginx 不会自动重新读取证书</strong>，部署后必须 reload。</li>\n<li><strong>Home Assistant 的 <code>X-Forwarded-*</code> 头会导致 400</strong>，其他服务的转发头不要随便加到 HA 的 vhost 上。</li>\n<li><strong>DNSPod 刷新有延迟</strong>，刚改完记录可能要等几分钟才能查到。</li>\n<li><strong>Nginx reload 要用 <code>nginx -s reload -c /etc/nginx/uci.conf</code></strong>，用 <code>/etc/init.d/nginx reload</code> 可能触发 iStore 的 SSL 自动生成逻辑。</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"相关地址\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#相关地址\" title=\"相关地址\"></a>相关地址</h2><ul>\n<li>ZeroTier 官网：<a href=\"https://www.zerotier.com/\" rel=\"noopener external nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.zerotier.com</a></li>\n<li>certd 官网：<a href=\"https://certd.docmirror.cn/\" rel=\"noopener external nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">https://certd.docmirror.cn</a></li>\n<li>DNSPod：<a href=\"https://console.dnspod.cn/\" rel=\"noopener external nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">https://console.dnspod.cn</a></li>\n<li>iStoreOS：<a href=\"https://www.istoreos.com/\" rel=\"noopener external nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.istoreos.com</a></li>\n<li>OpenWrt Wiki Nginx：<a href=\"https://openwrt.org/docs/guide-user/services/webserver/nginx\" rel=\"noopener external nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">https://openwrt.org/docs/guide-user/services/webserver/nginx</a></li>\n</ul>\n","i":"","t":"2026-09-02","p":"","n":0},"https://blog.zhheo.com/p/q6b3774w.html":{"c":"<p>我一直觉得，让 AI 只会聊天有点浪费。很多事情明明已经打开网页了，最后一步却还得我自己点：搜索、填写、切换页面、提交。</p>\n<p>BrowserSkill 做的事情很直接，让 AI 真正接入浏览器。</p>\n<p>它不是给浏览器套一个聊天窗口，而是通过 <code>bsk</code> CLI 和浏览器扩展建立连接，再让 AI 去观察页面、理解页面上的控件，然后执行点击、输入和选择等动作。</p>\n<h2 id=\"BrowserSkill-是怎么工作的\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#BrowserSkill-是怎么工作的\" title=\"BrowserSkill 是怎么工作的\"></a>BrowserSkill 是怎么工作的</h2><p>BrowserSkill 需要两个东西：一个是安装在电脑上的 <code>bsk</code> 命令行工具，另一个是加载到 Chromium 中的 browser-skill 扩展。扩展连接成功后，浏览器里会显示绿色状态。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"浏览器扩展\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/2708420260827104422.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"扩展窗口\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/5725320260827104440.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<p>AI 发起任务时，BrowserSkill 会打开一个独立的 Agent Window。这个窗口和用户正在使用的浏览器窗口分开，AI 默认只操作自己的标签页。需要操作用户现有页面时，也可以先把指定标签页借用进来，完成后再归还。</p>\n<p>这个隔离设计我比较喜欢。AI 要跑网页任务，就让它在自己的窗口里跑，不会突然把我正在看的网页刷新掉。</p>\n<h2 id=\"先观察，再操作\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#先观察，再操作\" title=\"先观察，再操作\"></a>先观察，再操作</h2><p>BrowserSkill 的基本工作流是：</p>\n<figure class=\"highlight text\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/><span class=\"line\">2</span><br/><span class=\"line\">3</span><br/><span class=\"line\">4</span><br/><span class=\"line\">5</span><br/><span class=\"line\">6</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\">bsk session start</span><br/><span class=\"line\">bsk observe</span><br/><span class=\"line\">bsk snapshot</span><br/><span class=\"line\">bsk click / fill / select</span><br/><span class=\"line\">bsk observe</span><br/><span class=\"line\">bsk session stop</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<p><code>observe</code> 用来获取页面的语义信息，能看到页面文字、按钮、输入框以及可交互控件。<code>snapshot</code> 则是更严格的无障碍树快照，适合在页面结构比较复杂时使用。</p>\n<p>AI 先观察页面，再根据按钮名称或输入框的作用执行操作。网页改版后，元素位置可能变了，但只要按钮文字和页面结构没有完全改变，AI 仍然有机会找到正确的目标。</p>\n<p>当然，它也不是开了挂。验证码、登录、短信验证和支付确认这类步骤，还是应该停下来交给人处理。任务完成后要及时结束 session，不要让 AI 长时间接管浏览器。</p>\n<h2 id=\"最有意思的功能：录制动作教-AI-学习\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#最有意思的功能：录制动作教-AI-学习\" title=\"最有意思的功能：录制动作教 AI 学习\"></a>最有意思的功能：录制动作教 AI 学习</h2><p>BrowserSkill 里我觉得最有意思的是 <code>bsk record</code>。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"功能按钮\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/4437920260827104524.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"操作录制\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/7472320260827104536.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<p>有些网页操作很难用语言描述。比如先打开某个后台，进入指定菜单，筛选日期，再点击导出。你可以写一大段说明，但 AI 还是可能漏掉中间某一步。</p>\n<p>这时候可以直接录制。</p>\n<p>指令可以让ai来操作。你填写完点击复制即可。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"操作指令\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/0237420260827104614.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<p>然后像平时一样操作网页，完成后点击录制面板里的 Finish。BrowserSkill 会生成一个 trace bundle，里面至少包含 <code>trace.json</code>，新版本还会保存 <code>states/</code> 目录。</p>\n<p><code>trace.json</code> 里有动作链，每一步还会关联操作前后的页面状态。<code>states/</code> 里保存页面观察结果，所以 AI 看到的不只是“点击了某个按钮”，还知道点击前页面长什么样、点击后页面发生了什么变化。</p>\n<p>这就像给 AI 做了一次网页演示。你先做一遍，它再根据记录理解流程，之后尝试复现。</p>\n<h2 id=\"录制适合哪些场景\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#录制适合哪些场景\" title=\"录制适合哪些场景\"></a>录制适合哪些场景</h2><p>重复执行的后台操作很适合录制，比如固定流程的数据导出、内容审核、订单查询，或者每周都要做一次的网页整理工作。</p>\n<p>录制完成后，可以把 trace 当成任务说明的一部分交给 AI。相比只说“帮我完成这个操作”，它多了真实的页面状态和动作顺序，出错时也更容易定位到底卡在了哪一步。</p>\n<p>不过录制时要注意隐私。不要在银行、单点登录、密码管理器等页面录制，也不要把包含敏感信息的 trace 随便发给别人。<code>--redact-values</code> 可以把表单值标记为 <code>[filled]</code> 或 <code>[empty]</code>，但涉及账号和密码的页面，最好还是直接避开。</p>\n<h2 id=\"我怎么看-BrowserSkill\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#我怎么看-BrowserSkill\" title=\"我怎么看 BrowserSkill\"></a>我怎么看 BrowserSkill</h2><p>以前让 AI 操作网页，通常要么依赖复杂的浏览器自动化脚本，要么只能把网页内容读出来，真正点击时还得自己补上。</p>\n<p>BrowserSkill 把这件事拆得比较清楚：session 负责生命周期，Agent Window 负责隔离，observe 和 snapshot 负责理解页面，click、fill、select 负责执行动作，record 则负责把人的操作变成 AI 可以参考的流程。</p>\n<p>尤其是录制功能，适合那些“我会做，但我懒得写教程”的任务。自己操作一遍，比对着网页截图解释半天省事多了。</p>\n<p>如果你平时经常登录后台、查资料、填表格，或者有一堆重复网页流程，BrowserSkill 值得试试。先从一个不涉及隐私的小任务开始，跑通之后再慢慢把常用流程录下来。</p>\n","i":"","t":"2026-09-02","p":"","n":0},"https://www.testingcatalog.com/google-develops-ai-rooms-for-gemini-enterprise/":{"c":"<html><body><div><section id=\"post-body\" class=\"post-body godo-canvas mx-auto relative font-serif\">\n        \n\n    <p>Google is prototyping a new Gemini Enterprise feature called Rooms, which could turn the platform into a shared workspace where teams collaborate with both colleagues and Gemini around a specific objective. TestingCatalog found references to the feature in recent Gemini Enterprise builds, but it remains marked as a prototype, and Google has not yet indicated plans to ship it publicly.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-image-card kg-width-wide\"><img src=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/2026/08/Gemini-Enterprise-08-31-2026_12_52_AM.jpg\" class=\"kg-image\" alt=\"Gemini\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w600/2026/08/Gemini-Enterprise-08-31-2026_12_52_AM.jpg 600w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1000/2026/08/Gemini-Enterprise-08-31-2026_12_52_AM.jpg 1000w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1600/2026/08/Gemini-Enterprise-08-31-2026_12_52_AM.jpg 1600w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w2400/2026/08/Gemini-Enterprise-08-31-2026_12_52_AM.jpg 2400w\" sizes=\"(min-width: 1200px) 1200px\"></figure><p>Rooms are described as an “all-in-one place” environment where Gemini becomes an expert using connected files while keeping team conversations focused. Creating one involves defining a goal, a playbook describing how Gemini should operate, and a knowledge base. Teams can then add members and files, maintain shared context, and communicate with each other or Gemini inside the same space.</p><p>The concept appears closely related to <a href=\"https://www.testingcatalog.com/google-expands-gemini-for-business-with-shareable-projects/\">Projects</a>, which Google publicly introduced at Cloud Next 2026 as shared workspaces for humans and agents. Projects already combine conversations with sources from services such as Google Workspace, Microsoft OneDrive, NotebookLM, and team chats. Rooms appear to take that idea further by giving the workspace an explicit objective, operating instructions, and a more structured knowledge layer.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-image-card kg-width-wide\"><img src=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/2026/08/Rooms-Gemini-Enterprise-08-31-2026_12_53_AM.jpg\" class=\"kg-image\" alt=\"Gemini\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w600/2026/08/Rooms-Gemini-Enterprise-08-31-2026_12_53_AM.jpg 600w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1000/2026/08/Rooms-Gemini-Enterprise-08-31-2026_12_53_AM.jpg 1000w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1600/2026/08/Rooms-Gemini-Enterprise-08-31-2026_12_53_AM.jpg 1600w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w2400/2026/08/Rooms-Gemini-Enterprise-08-31-2026_12_53_AM.jpg 2400w\" sizes=\"(min-width: 1200px) 1200px\"></figure><p>For enterprise teams, this could position Gemini closer to project management and operational collaboration software rather than serving primarily as an assistant layered over company data. One particularly useful direction would be connecting context gathered during Google Meet calls with room decisions, documentation, tasks, and ongoing conversations, although there is currently no evidence that Meet integration is part of the prototype.</p><p>Google has been steadily repositioning <a href=\"https://www.testingcatalog.com/tag/gemini/\">Gemini</a> Enterprise as an agentic workplace platform, with long-running agents, Projects, Canvas, an Agent Gallery, enterprise connectors, and persistent agent memory all forming parts of that strategy. Recent interface changes point in the same direction: the Customization area is being reorganized to include dedicated Agents and Memory sections, with agents potentially moving into a list where users can inspect and configure them.</p><p>For now, Rooms remain an internal prototype. Their final name, availability, supported data sources, and whether they will replace or coexist with Projects are still unclear.</p>\n</section>\n\n\n\n\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1200/2026/08/Rooms-Gemini-Enterprise-08-31-2026_12_51_AM--1-.jpg","t":"2026-09-02","p":"","n":0},"https://blog.zhheo.com/p/npa0251o.html":{"c":"<p>OpenClaw凉了的话太多了，自从Hermes出完之后，OpenClaw凉了、没人用的话真的太多人讲了。天天刷自媒体全是这些东西。</p>\n<p>有的时候我也被迫焦虑住了，比如OpenClaw更新频率现在很低了。一个月才出一个正式版。Hermes还有好用的mac客户端等等。我已经不止一次下载了Hermes并且安装，但是我总是在最后一步又放弃了。</p>\n<p>我怀疑是不是老了不爱研究了。最近看到差评的<a href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1DWGK6PE9r?vd_source=590d6de9563ef4d8076365304a66699e\" rel=\"noopener external nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">OpenClaw都凉透了，我却花140天把隐私全交给它，蒸馏出了真正可用的赛博秘书。</a></p>\n<p>我也就释然了。</p>\n<p>这个视频帮助我回答了几个问题，然后反思。OpenClaw确实凉了，但OpenClaw确实是最适合我的方式，我也没必要硬换。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Hermes自进化\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#Hermes自进化\" title=\"Hermes自进化\"></a>Hermes自进化</h2><p>Hermes很多人宣传各种自进化，我其实能够理解，因为在涉及一些skill操作时，如果我观察到路径很长，我会提醒OpenClaw让他去优化修改skill。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"手动询问\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/6112820260827051127.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<p>这个步骤在Hermes中应该是可以自动完成的，不需要我手动提醒。</p>\n<p>但是这也会让我很担心。比如skill的一些脚本会不会因为某次的错误操作、错误行为且正确完成后因为自进化而被迫修改了。在我不知道的时候自己偷偷改掉了之类的。</p>\n<p>OpenClaw的skill就像是我写好的程序，我可以随时去重新编辑优化。而如果是自进化，那么在我眼里就是个黑箱了。skill的创建到维护都成了黑箱。</p>\n<p>视频里说的一个观点对也不对，但是成功帮我驱散了迷雾。</p>\n<p>他说Hermes是基于skill自进化，OpenClaw是基于记忆的自进化。</p>\n<p>但是基于记忆很难说上是自进化，因为Hermes也有记忆，但是虽然说的不好，但是让我确定了。</p>\n<p>我其实并不需要Hermes的自进化，我有记忆就够了。</p>\n<h2 id=\"OpenClaw确实能解决问题\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#OpenClaw确实能解决问题\" title=\"OpenClaw确实能解决问题\"></a>OpenClaw确实能解决问题</h2><p>像是我这种活在互联网的人，OpenClaw能解决我生活中的很大部分问题。</p>\n<p>比如昨天晚上我平板无法在应用商店下载东西了，OpenClaw直接去访问我软路由，联网查，然后找到工具添加覆写规则。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"查看规则\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/5775420260827051124.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<p>比如我homeassistant有一些配置项出问题了，OpenClaw直接访问我homeassistant帮我改、帮我调参数，帮我建实体，帮我重启。</p>\n<p>我觉得用什么工具不重要，重要的是实现。</p>\n<p>OpenClaw已经实现了AI帮我解决互联网问题的需求，即使换到Hermes，也只是完成同样的需求。可能在不同场景下各有优劣，但结果都能完成。</p>\n<p>所以我不再产生OpenClaw焦虑了。即使OpenClaw凉了，没有人用了，但是我还是会用的。除非有颠覆性的新产品了。</p>\n<p>openclaw比我vibecoding省token多了，只用它来做助手，基本上不用担心。一个月才花了8亿左右。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"消耗量\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/7753620260827051119.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<p>最近mac端我用上了ClawX客户端，对话不卡顿还不错。啥时候官方有mac客户端就好了。</p>\n","i":"","t":"2026-09-02","p":"","n":0},"https://blog.zhheo.com/p/ucrz6hhg.html":{"c":"<p>Windows 移动硬盘插到 Mac 上能读不能写，这个老问题到现在都没有官方解法。以前想写入，要么装内核扩展（新版 SIP 政策基本把这条路堵死了），要么花钱买付费驱动。</p>\n<p>ntfsmac 走了第三条路，思路挺野：起一个 Linux 虚拟机来替 macOS 干活。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"nfcmac\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/1304420260824053900.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"原理\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#原理\" title=\"原理\"></a>原理</h2><p>它用 libkrun 运行一个一次性的 Linux 微虚拟机，里面跑 ntfs-3g，真正的 NTFS 写入都在虚拟机里完成，然后通过一块仅主机可达的 vmnet 虚拟网卡，以 NFS 方式挂回 macOS。</p>\n<figure class=\"highlight plaintext\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\">macOS ── NFS ──&gt; vmnet 桥接 ──&gt; libkrun 微虚拟机 ── ntfs-3g ──&gt; NTFS 硬盘</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<p>全程没有内核扩展，不关 SIP，也不用去系统设置里批准系统扩展，对越来越严的新版 macOS 来说省心不少。</p>\n<p>顺带一提，ext2/ext3/ext4 分区也能挂。用的是 Linux 内核自带的驱动，blkid 自动识别类型，连参数都不用指定。ext 文件系统自带权限位，它会自动帮你忽略权限，挂载后文件直接归你、可写。</p>\n<p>多块盘同时挂也没问题，GUI 里每块盘单独显示状态和速度。</p>\n<h2 id=\"性能和占用\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#性能和占用\" title=\"性能和占用\"></a>性能和占用</h2><p>挂载速度不用担心，这不是传统虚拟机那种要等半天开机的路子。Linux 被裁剪得很彻底，连 UEFI 固件都没有，命令下去几秒钟盘就挂好了。</p>\n<p>内存是真开销：每块盘对应一个虚拟机，默认内存上限 512MB，典型实际占用 256MB 左右。M 系列的统一内存扛这点没压力，但要是一口气挂四五块盘，自己心里得有数。</p>\n<p>还有两个网络驱动器的副作用提前说：macOS 会把挂载盘认成 NFS 网络盘，平时无感，但 Microsoft Word 没法直接编辑里面的文档（Word 对网络文件系统的老毛病）；另外长时间大量拷贝小文件时，默认的 ntfs-3g 配这套 NFS 偶尔会报 I/O 错误，重试一般都能过。</p>\n<h2 id=\"安装和使用\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#安装和使用\" title=\"安装和使用\"></a>安装和使用</h2><p><a href=\"https://github.com/khr898/ntfsmac/releases\" rel=\"noopener external nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">https://github.com/khr898/ntfsmac/releases</a></p>\n<p>嫌 GitHub 下载慢的，我也传了一份到国内网盘（v2.2.160826，58.8MB，和 Release 原包一致）：</p>\n<p>百度网盘：<a href=\"https://pan.baidu.com/s/1f-gSXa4i5BQt0Ge5xE9auQ?pwd=56qn\" rel=\"noopener external nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">https://pan.baidu.com/s/1f-gSXa4i5BQt0Ge5xE9auQ?pwd=56qn</a></p>\n<p>夸克网盘：<a href=\"https://pan.quark.cn/s/9595b09061d6?pwd=08h9\" rel=\"noopener external nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">https://pan.quark.cn/s/9595b09061d6?pwd=08h9</a></p>\n<p>装完是个菜单栏应用，没有 Dock 图标。图标颜色就是状态：灰是空闲，蓝在挂载中，绿说明已经读写挂载成功，黄是只读（日志脏了），红代表出错。</p>\n<p>遇到问题先跑 <code>ntfsmac diagnose</code>，只读检查环境，不会碰你的盘。</p>\n<h2 id=\"几个要知道的点\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#几个要知道的点\" title=\"几个要知道的点\"></a>几个要知道的点</h2><p>只支持 Apple Silicon，Intel Mac 无缘；系统要求 macOS 13 以上。</p>\n<p>第一次挂载需要联网，会下载一个锁定了 SHA-256 摘要的 Alpine 镜像（50 到 150MB）。之后同版本缓存离线可用，不用重复下载。</p>\n<p>权限方面，GUI 第一次挂载会申请「完全磁盘访问」，给一次就行。CLI 只有在你需要从终端往盘里复制文件时才要给 Terminal 开这个权限，只用 Finder 读写就不用管。</p>\n<h2 id=\"写在最后\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#写在最后\" title=\"写在最后\"></a>写在最后</h2><p>M 系列芯片的 Mac，经常要读写 NTFS 或 ext 移动硬盘，又不想关 SIP、不想为写入功能付钱的话，值得一试。仓库地址：</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/khr898/ntfsmac\" rel=\"noopener external nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">https://github.com/khr898/ntfsmac</a></p>\n","i":"","t":"2026-09-02","p":"","n":0},"https://workspaces.beehiiv.com/p/252-jack-raines":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"_10pdwo80 dream-post-content-doc\"><div class=\"_1gqvddm0\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">He also edits Litquidity's daily finance newsletter, </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://www.execsum.co/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Exec Sum</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">.</span></p></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">He does all of this while being an MBA candidate at Columbia Business School.</span></p></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Fun facts: He's been deported from Norway, learned how to salsa dance in Argentina, and almost got kicked out of business school for a </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jackraines/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">satirical LinkedIn post</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">.</span></p></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What is the gear in your workspace?</span></h2></p><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What is your favorite item in your workspace?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">My Xebec. It's portable and triples my screen size.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">How do you spark creativity?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">I've never sparked creativity, it sparks me. Creativity usually hits when I'm in the gym, or on the subway, or at a dive bar at 1 AM. When it does hit, I text myself a few blurbs to review later when I'm by my computer.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">How do you manage work-life balance?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">The best way to manage work-life balance is work on stuff that you don't feel the need to balance.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What does your typical writing process look like?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">I sit down, write for 15 minutes, hop on Twitter to look for a tweet that I want to reference, procrastinate on Twitter for 20 minutes, throw my phone on my bed, close Twitter, grind on the newsletter some more.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></body></html>","i":"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,quality=80,width=1200,onerror=redirect/uploads/asset/file/2fbcbb73-0bf8-4377-a108-4ac404a2b846/image.png?t=1781141971","t":"2026-09-02","p":"","n":0},"https://www.testingcatalog.com/perplexity-prepares-hybrid-mode-for-computer-on-mac/":{"c":"<html><body><div><section id=\"post-body\" class=\"post-body godo-canvas mx-auto relative font-serif\">\n        \n\n    <p>Perplexity is preparing to bring local inference to a much wider group of Mac users through a new Hybrid Mode for Perplexity Computer. The company previously announced hybrid agentic inference in June and said support would extend beyond Windows to Macs and Linux. More recently, it launched Portable Computer for NVIDIA DGX Spark, where Computer can run entirely on local hardware.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-embed-card\">\n</figure><p>On Mac, the implementation appears different. Hybrid Mode lets Computer continue orchestrating in the cloud while automatically delegating suitable subtasks to a model running locally. Cloud models handle heavier reasoning, while local inference handles lighter work without consuming Computer credits and keeps the associated data on the Mac.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-image-card kg-width-wide\"><img src=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-30-at-01.00.39.png\" class=\"kg-image\" alt=\"Perplexity\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w600/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-30-at-01.00.39.png 600w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1000/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-30-at-01.00.39.png 1000w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1600/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-30-at-01.00.39.png 1600w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w2400/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-30-at-01.00.39.png 2400w\" sizes=\"(min-width: 1200px) 1200px\"></figure><figure class=\"kg-card kg-image-card kg-width-wide\"><img src=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-30-at-00.59.13.png\" class=\"kg-image\" alt=\"Perplexity\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w600/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-30-at-00.59.13.png 600w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1000/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-30-at-00.59.13.png 1000w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1600/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-30-at-00.59.13.png 1600w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w2400/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-30-at-00.59.13.png 2400w\" sizes=\"(min-width: 1200px) 1200px\"></figure><p>Users can enable Hybrid Mode from the Computer model selector and configure local inference if no model is installed. Three downloadable options are currently being prepared: a recommended Perplexity model around 19 GB requiring at least 32 GB of memory, a roughly 17.4 GB Qwen 32B option with similar requirements, and a smaller Gemma-based model around 5.6 GB that can run on 16 GB Macs. The exact identity of Perplexity's own model remains unclear.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-image-card kg-width-wide\"><img src=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-31-at-00.45.36.png\" class=\"kg-image\" alt=\"Perplexity\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w600/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-31-at-00.45.36.png 600w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1000/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-31-at-00.45.36.png 1000w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1600/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-31-at-00.45.36.png 1600w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w2400/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-31-at-00.45.36.png 2400w\" sizes=\"(min-width: 1200px) 1200px\"></figure><p>Another feature, Privacy Gate, adds a separate local model that inspects data before it is sent to the cloud. If it detects personal or sensitive information, Computer can ask the user how to handle it before transmission. This could be particularly relevant to users and companies operating under GDPR requirements in the EEA.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-image-card kg-width-wide\"><img src=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-31-at-00.45.05.png\" class=\"kg-image\" alt=\"Perplexity\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w600/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-31-at-00.45.05.png 600w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1000/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-31-at-00.45.05.png 1000w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1600/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-31-at-00.45.05.png 1600w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w2400/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-31-at-00.45.05.png 2400w\" sizes=\"(min-width: 1200px) 1200px\"></figure><p>Computer is evolving from a cloud-only agent into an orchestration layer spanning cloud infrastructure and user-controlled hardware. The company has already publicly described this architecture as hybrid agentic inference, positioning local processing around privacy and lower inference costs while retaining access to frontier models.</p><p>The Mac controls described here remain hidden, and <a href=\"https://www.testingcatalog.com/tag/perplexity/\">Perplexity</a> has not announced their release date or whether access will be limited by subscription tier. A fully local Mac orchestrator, similar to Portable Computer on DGX Spark, also does not appear to be confirmed yet.</p>\n</section>\n\n\n\n\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1200/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-30-at-01.00.28.png","t":"2026-09-02","p":"","n":0},"https://workspaces.beehiiv.com/p/253-david-heinemeier-hansson":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"_10pdwo80 dream-post-content-doc\"><div class=\"_1gqvddm0\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">He is the creator of </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://rubyonrails.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Ruby on Rails</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, the open-source framework that has been used by hundreds of thousands of developers.</span></p></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">And if that wasn't enough, he's also a </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://dhh.dk/#driver\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">race car driver</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> in the FIA World Endurance Championship.</span></p></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What does your typical day look like?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Early mornings are spent getting kids to school. I usually sit down to work around 8:30. Then it's typically an hour or so catching up on emails, reports, whatever. Then the very best days are entirely free from there to dive into interesting, challenging projects, preferably programming or writing.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What do you think are the main benefits of remote work in 2023?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">I've been working remotely for twenty years, and the benefits remain the same for me. The freedom to live wherever, to work from a home office that provides complete calm for focus, and to enjoy the flexibility of being literally next door to the family during the day. Wouldn't trade it for anything.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">How do you personally balance work between multiple ongoing projects?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">I try to work in seasons. Some seasons are dedicated to programming others to writing and others still to working on the business itself. Multitasking is a mirage. All humans can do is thrash. So keeping just one main project on the plate at the time is the key to going quickly.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></body></html>","i":"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,quality=80,width=1200,onerror=redirect/uploads/asset/file/269219fe-657a-455e-9fce-87aaafb183ec/image.png?t=1781141716","t":"2026-09-02","p":"","n":0},"https://www.testingcatalog.com/google-prepares-interactive-reports-for-gemini-notebook/":{"c":"<html><body><div><section id=\"post-body\" class=\"post-body godo-canvas mx-auto relative font-serif\">\n        \n\n    <p>Google is preparing another major addition to Gemini Notebook called Interactive Reports. A new notice has appeared in the Studio panel stating, “New: you can now create interactive reports,” with a button that opens the existing Create Report customization flow. This type of release messaging suggests Google is already preparing the feature for users, potentially within the coming weeks.</p><p>Inside the report creator, a new “Interactive” option is marked as New and described as “An interactive report with embedded Studio content.” Another preset, “Overview,” can create an interactive summary of key information while incorporating Studio content directly into the result.</p><p>Users can select a language and provide detailed instructions describing the report they want. Google’s example asks for a formal competitive review of the 2026 functional beverage market, covering competitors, distribution, and pricing to support a launch strategy. This points toward research-heavy use cases where Gemini Notebook combines multiple sources into something closer to a structured research workspace than a static document.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-image-card kg-width-wide\"><img src=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/2026/08/Gemini-Notebook-08-30-2026_12_12_AM.jpg\" class=\"kg-image\" alt=\"Gemini Notebook\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w600/2026/08/Gemini-Notebook-08-30-2026_12_12_AM.jpg 600w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1000/2026/08/Gemini-Notebook-08-30-2026_12_12_AM.jpg 1000w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1600/2026/08/Gemini-Notebook-08-30-2026_12_12_AM.jpg 1600w, https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w2400/2026/08/Gemini-Notebook-08-30-2026_12_12_AM.jpg 2400w\" sizes=\"(min-width: 1200px) 1200px\"></figure><p>The exact types of Studio content that can be embedded remain unclear. Previous builds also contained placeholders for <a href=\"https://www.testingcatalog.com/google-tests-canvas-and-connectors-on-notebooklm/\">Canvas</a> and <a href=\"https://www.testingcatalog.com/google-is-working-on-interactive-apps-for-gemini-notebook/\">Web Page</a> outputs, resembling the artifact-style experiences available elsewhere in Gemini. Those concepts could remain separate, or some of that work may now be converging into Interactive Reports.</p><p>The feature fits Google’s broader direction for Gemini Notebook. In July, Google expanded Studio beyond traditional summaries with support for generated documents, charts, spreadsheets, presentations and other editable outputs, while positioning Notebook as a research environment capable of handling more complex projects.</p><p>Interactive Reports would push that strategy further by combining generated research with other Studio outputs inside one report. If the current release notice reflects Google’s rollout plans, this may be one of the next <a href=\"https://www.testingcatalog.com/tag/notebooklm/\">Gemini Notebook</a> features to surface publicly.</p>\n</section>\n\n\n\n\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1200/2026/08/Gemini-Notebook-08-30-2026_12_10_AM.jpg","t":"2026-09-02","p":"","n":0},"https://www.testingcatalog.com/first-outputs-from-gpt-6-astra-model-from-openai/":{"c":"<html><body><div><section id=\"post-body\" class=\"post-body godo-canvas mx-auto relative font-serif\">\n        \n\n    <p>OpenAI appears to be moving Astra closer to release, with reports pointing to expanded internal testing and a new checkpoint identified as ‚Äúmozaik-alpha-fdm.‚Äù The latest surfaced outputs were reportedly generated zero-shot with Max effort, where Astra spends substantially longer reasoning than GPT-5.6 Sol.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-video-card kg-width-wide kg-card-hascaption\" data-kg-thumbnail=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/media/2026/08/astra1_thumb.jpg\" data-kg-custom-thumbnail=\"\">\n            \n            <figcaption><p><span>Voxel Castle output from Astra</span></p></figcaption>\n        </figure><p>The examples point to a strong focus on coding and visual software creation. Astra reportedly produced a GTA 2-style game in one attempt, alongside detailed websites, 3D objects, and voxel environments. The main difference visible in these samples is attention to small implementation details and the amount of complete functionality produced from a single prompt. Developers, designers, and founders building prototypes could be among the main beneficiaries if this performance carries over to the released model.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-embed-card\">\n</figure><p>Astra could arrive through <a href=\"https://www.testingcatalog.com/tag/chatgpt/\">ChatGPT</a>, Codex or both, especially given OpenAI's focus on agentic coding and long-running work. OpenAI has not announced a release date or confirmed that ‚Äúmozaik-alpha-fdm‚Äù is an official codename. Separate reports have suggested a launch within weeks, while the newly expanded testing provides another indication that preparations are progressing.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-embed-card\">\n</figure><p>One major variable remains timing: safety approval. OpenAI has officially acknowledged Astra as an upcoming model and said its internal evaluations showed major advances in agentic coding and cybersecurity, potentially reaching its Critical cyber capability threshold. Some Astra workloads were subsequently paused while stricter safeguards were introduced. OpenAI has also confirmed that relevant government agencies and selected AI safety organizations will participate in testing.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-embed-card\">\n</figure><figure class=\"kg-card kg-embed-card\">\n</figure><p>This makes government evaluation part of the actual deployment process rather than simply another rumor. It also means a technically ready Astra may still remain gated until OpenAI is satisfied with its monitoring, alignment, and containment systems.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-embed-card\">\n</figure><p>Meanwhile, several people with histories of early access to frontier models have hinted that Astra represents a much larger capability jump than recent <a href=\"https://www.testingcatalog.com/tag/openai/\">OpenAI</a> releases. GPT-6 remains a plausible public name, but OpenAI has given no indication that it has chosen this branding.</p><p>Source: <a href=\"https://discord.gg/3Km9qnH6D?ref=testingcatalog.com\">zAI Discord</a></p>\n</section>\n\n\n\n\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1200/2026/08/SEO_Banner_2560x1440_02--1--1.jpg","t":"2026-09-01","p":"","n":0},"https://www.testingcatalog.com/tencent-released-open-source-hy4-preview-model/":{"c":"<html><body><div><section id=\"post-body\" class=\"post-body godo-canvas mx-auto relative font-serif\">\n        \n\n    <p>Tencent has released Hy4 preview, a 770-billion-parameter flagship model with 49 billion active parameters and a one-million-token context window. The company calls it its most capable model so far and says it delivers the largest generation-over-generation gain it has measured. The open-source release targets long-horizon software engineering, document-heavy office work, game development and scientific research.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-embed-card\">\n</figure><p>For software projects, Hy4 preview is designed to understand, plan, debug and verify work across extended sessions, with added focus on the visual quality of front-end output. It can also turn scattered files into documents, spreadsheets and presentations, including work involving data analysis, equations and financial models. Tencent says the model can build playable prototypes from one prompt and continue refining complex projects in game engines over multiple turns. Its research scope includes AI, condensed matter physics and pure mathematics.</p><p>In one test, Hy4 preview managed several Codex sessions in parallel and changed its research direction as results arrived. On a small-model post-training task, it coordinated work across several evaluation targets and beat Codex working independently on all eight benchmarks, according to Tencent. The company presents this as evidence that the model can judge research direction, organize experiments, and iterate on complex R&amp;D work.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-video-card kg-width-wide\" data-kg-thumbnail=\"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/media/2026/08/hy4_thumb.jpg\" data-kg-custom-thumbnail=\"\">\n            \n            \n        </figure><p>A blind internal comparison involved 163 Tencent experts rating outputs across 203 engineering tasks. Hy4 preview averaged 2.99, slightly above GLM 5.3 (2.92) and Kimi K3 (2.94). Against GLM 5.3, it recorded 46.8% wins, 12.8% ties, and 40.4% losses. Against Kimi K3, it posted 51.2% wins, 7.9% ties and 40.9% losses.</p><p>Tencent built Hy4 preview with training data shaped around work performed by its software engineers, game developers, finance analysts, and security experts. It continues to co-design the model with CodeBuddy and WorkBuddy, while access is available through Tencent Cloud, OpenRouter, Yuanbao, ima, and public repositories. API pricing per million tokens is $0.042 for cached input, $0.834 for input, and $2.501 for output. Tencent describes Hy4 preview as an early version and acknowledges that it can reason longer than needed on complex tasks and over-verify its own work.</p><p><a href=\"https://hy.tencent.ai/research/hy4-preview?ref=testingcatalog.com\">Source</a></p>\n</section>\n\n\n\n\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1200/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-29-at-14.24.40.png","t":"2026-09-01","p":"","n":0},"https://www.cnbeta.com.tw/articles/tech/1575806.htm":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"article-content\" id=\"artibody\">\n                        <p class=\"article-global\"></p>                            <p><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/30b5068dbc04c75.webp\" title=\"\" alt=\"image.webp\"></p><p>Firefox 155支持Happy Eyeballs v3，可同时尝试多种连接方式，并优先采用最先成功的连接。该机制在并行比较IPv4与IPv6的基础上，还能利用现代DNS记录识别服务器支持的协议，并同时尝试HTTP/2和HTTP/3，从而寻找速度更快的连接路径。</p><p>新版本还支持HTTP/3连接使用QUIC v2。当服务器通过兼容的版本协商选择QUIC v2时，Firefox将自动采用该协议。</p><p>Firefox 155新增了可选的Smart Window功能。这是一种由人工智能驱动的桌面浏览窗口，在获得用户授权后，可以访问已打开的标签页和浏览历史。目前，Smart Window仅面向美国、加拿大和法国用户提供。</p><p><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/e3233b472020741.webp\" title=\"\" alt=\"image-1.webp\"></p><p>此外，新版本修复了一个可能导致Linux系统在长时间浏览后无法进入睡眠状态的问题。</p><p>面向开发者，Firefox 155加入了多项更新，包括支持WebAssembly Compact Import Section、支持用于128位算术指令的WebAssembly Wide Arithmetic，将font-stretch的标准属性名称调整为font-width，改善WebRTC互操作性，并支持progress() CSS函数。</p><p>Firefox 155的发布版本现已可从ftp.mozilla.org下载：</p><p><a href=\"https://ftp.mozilla.org/pub/firefox/releases/155.0/\" _src=\"https://ftp.mozilla.org/pub/firefox/releases/155.0/\" target=\"_blank\">https://ftp.mozilla.org/pub/firefox/releases/155.0/</a></p>                        </div>\n                    </div></body></html>","i":"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/30b5068dbc04c75.webp","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.cnbeta.com.tw/articles/tech/1575804.htm":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"article-content\" id=\"artibody\">\n                        <p class=\"article-global\"></p>                            <p><a href=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0804/9c8098c2cd096a3.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0804/9c8098c2cd096a3.jpg\"></a></p><p>诉状称，亚马逊违反了《联邦贸易委员会法》以及十多项州法律。案件发生在亚马逊同意支付25亿美元、就Prime订阅业务相关指控达成和解近一年之后。</p><p>亚马逊广告通常采用“第二价格”竞价机制，即获胜广告主原则上只需支付比第二高出价者高出一美分的价格。然而，FTC指控称，自2019年以来，亚马逊一直在操纵这一竞价流程。</p><p>据诉状，亚马逊广告部门会在竞价结束、确定最高和第二高出价后，用一套旨在最大化公司利润、降低广告投放成本效率的更高价格，替换原本由竞价决定的价格。亚马逊广告部门负责人的内部表述显示，所谓“第二价格”并非由实际竞价者决定，而是由亚马逊计算出的“代理第二价格”。</p><p>FTC认为，这一做法可能在广告主不知情的情况下非法收取超过200亿美元。亚马逊则发表声明，称FTC的诉讼“误导且缺乏依据”，并表示FTC“根本误解了广告主的行为”。亚马逊还称，2019年至2024年，Sponsored Products搜索广告的平均获胜出价下降了50%。</p>                        </div>\n                    </div></body></html>","i":"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0804/9c8098c2cd096a3.jpg","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.cnbeta.com.tw/articles/tech/1575802.htm":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"article-content\" id=\"artibody\">\n                        <p class=\"article-global\"></p>                            <p><a href=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0630/d0bf21eec30bed0.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0630/d0bf21eec30bed0.jpg\"></a></p><p>苹果于今年7月首次提起诉讼，指控多名前员工窃取商业秘密，并将相关信息提供给OpenAI。数周后，苹果申请初步禁令，同时要求法院加快证据调查，包括提前提交文件，并对OpenAI的关键员工及高管进行询问。上周，苹果再次强调加快调查的必要性。OpenAI则要求法院驳回诉讼。</p><p>刘畅是苹果诉讼中列名的被告之一。他此前是苹果公司的高级系统电气工程师，于今年1月离职并加入OpenAI。苹果在诉讼中指控，刘畅利用一项安全漏洞，在离职后下载了苹果的机密工程文件。</p><p>苹果在最新文件中称，刘畅的律师近期交还了他离开苹果后使用的一台MacBook。苹果表示，对这台电脑进行“初步取证分析”后发现了四项情况。</p><p><strong>第一，刘畅不仅下载了苹果的一份机密电路原理图，还在OpenAI的工作中使用了该文件。</strong></p><p><strong>第二，刘畅及OpenAI的其他人员并非不知道他未经授权访问苹果第三方云存储这一事实，相反，他们对此十分清楚。</strong></p><p><strong>第三，刘畅得知苹果正在对他展开内部调查后，向一名OpenAI同事发出了销毁证据的指示；对方则确认会照办。</strong></p><p><strong>第四，刘畅在OpenAI工作中使用的一款工具，与苹果内部用于开发工作的工程应用程序同名。</strong></p><p>苹果称，刘畅曾在今年3月使用这份电路原理图，在LTspice这一电气工程工具中运行模拟程序。大约在同一时期的消息中，刘畅表示，他的人工智能“代理”已经学会运行LTspice并审查模拟结果。</p><p>苹果据此认为，当商业秘密被输入一个能够从相关信息中学习的人工智能代理或模型后，这种学习过程“可能造成对商业秘密不可逆且持续扩散的使用”。</p><p>苹果还表示，被告方面决定不对这台MacBook进行检查，反而选择提出一些“已被设备数据证明并不成立的说法”。</p><p>此外，苹果称，之所以发现刘畅使用过这份电路原理图，是因为他曾在一台Mac mini上使用该文件，而这台Mac mini后来通过iCloud与他从苹果带走的MacBook进行了同步。苹果目前也希望获得对这台Mac mini的访问权限。</p><p>苹果认为，这些“惊人证据”进一步证明了加快证据调查的必要性。苹果在提交文件中表示：“被告明明可以获得这些惊人证据，却选择置之不理。这充分说明苹果为何迫切需要加快证据调查。MacBook所呈现的，只是被告迄今为止提供的极其有限的信息，而且这些信息还是在拖延数周后才提交的。相关证据表明，苹果并非在进行无根据的‘钓鱼式调查’，而是有确切理由认为其商业秘密正在被使用，且相关证据正在遭到销毁。”</p><p>苹果提交的完整文件可通过法院记录或相关链接查阅。</p>                        </div>\n                    </div></body></html>","i":"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0630/d0bf21eec30bed0.jpg","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.cnbeta.com.tw/articles/tech/1575800.htm":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"article-content\" id=\"artibody\">\n                        <p class=\"article-global\"></p>                            <p>GenAI.mil于去年启用，最初接入Google <a href=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2025/0413/f0c2196c6924247.webp\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2025/0413/f0c2196c6924247.webp\"></a>Gemini，旨在让国防部工作人员通过集中化、安全的渠道使用商业前沿人工智能模型，避免敏感政府数据经过普通消费者服务传输。与面向公众的产品不同，军方版本不纳入消费级科技产品中难以规避的数据收集机制。</p><p>据美国国防部统计，GenAI.mil目前已吸引超过170万名独立用户，约占国防部300万名人员的一半以上。</p><p>ChatGPT Mil由OpenAI政府业务项目推出，整体使用体验将接近商业版ChatGPT，主要支持聊天、文件处理、项目管理和定制GPT等功能。国防部表示，该工具将首先服务于文件密集型、常规且不涉密的工作，包括行政事务、后勤、规划和政策制定，未来还会逐步增加更多功能。</p><p>相比之下，五角大楼对Grok for Government的定位更加广泛，并强调其军事和作战用途。美国国防部称，该工具将帮助作战人员提升工作效率、加强知识延续能力，并促进更安全、高效的协作，从而在多种行动环境中以更快速度和更高精度执行任务。</p><p>相关应用范围包括为采购人员开展市场研究分析，以及帮助后勤人员进行供应链管理。Grok for Government由SpaceX旗下Starshield AI提供。Starshield是面向安全场景的卫星网络，采用了Starlink的相关技术。</p><p>此次引入ChatGPT Mil和Grok，也反映出五角大楼在人工智能领域持续扩大合作范围，同时凸显了Anthropic旗下Claude模型的缺席。此前，Anthropic因拒绝给予美国国防部不受限制的人工智能工具使用权限，并坚持设置特定安全护栏，与五角大楼发生争议。特朗普政府随后将Anthropic认定为供应链风险企业，而该公司目前正通过法律途径挑战这一认定。</p><p>除OpenAI和xAI外，美国国防部还与亚马逊云服务、微软、英伟达以及Reflection AI等科技公司达成合作，希望进一步提升其人工智能能力，在确保安全的前提下加快工作流程，并增强美国国防体系的技术优势。</p>                        </div>\n                    </div></body></html>","i":"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2025/0413/f0c2196c6924247.webp","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.cnbeta.com.tw/articles/tech/1575798.htm":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"article-content\" id=\"artibody\">\n                        <p class=\"article-global\"></p>                            <p><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/b06727aeaeaf7be.jpg\"></p><p>苹果于今年7月起诉Chang Liu和Tang Tan，称两人通过多种方式获取苹果数据。Chang Liu离职后保留了一台由苹果配发的MacBook，苹果在诉讼启动后收回该设备，并从取证分析中发现了更多相关证据。</p><p>苹果在提交的文件中表示，Chang Liu不仅下载了机密电路原理图，还将其用于OpenAI的工作；他和OpenAI的其他人员明知自己仍能未经授权访问苹果的第三方云存储；在得知苹果正在展开内部调查后，他曾向一名OpenAI同事发出销毁证据的指示，对方还确认会照做。此外，Chang Liu在OpenAI使用的一款工具，与苹果内部用于工程开发的应用程序同名。</p><p>据苹果称，Chang Liu在离开公司约两个月后的今年3月下载了这份电路原理图，并使用LTspice电气工程软件进行模拟。他随后向他人透露，自己已经让一个AI代理学会运行LTspice、查看结果并调整补偿参数，以开展电源转换相关开发工作。Chang Liu表示，原本需要一天完成的工作，在AI代理学习后可以压缩到约两小时。</p><p>这份原理图曾在一台Mac mini上使用，随后与Chang Liu带走的MacBook进行了同步，因此苹果得以发现相关活动。苹果目前还希望调查Chang Liu仍持有的Mac mini及其他设备。</p><p>苹果认为，这些证据表明其商业机密正在被实际使用，同时相关证据可能遭到销毁，因此有必要加快取证。苹果此前还申请限制OpenAI使用其商业机密的禁令。</p><p>OpenAI则要求法院驳回诉讼，称苹果的指控“毫无根据”。该公司还发表声明，批评苹果的诉讼“草率、咄咄逼人且带有不同寻常的个人色彩”，并表示自己既没有、也不希望拥有苹果的商业机密，更关注于开发推动技术边界的创新产品和技术。</p><p>法官爱德华·J·达维拉计划于10月1日听取双方在此案中的陈述。</p>                        </div>\n                    </div></body></html>","i":"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/b06727aeaeaf7be.jpg","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.cnbeta.com.tw/articles/tech/1575796.htm":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"article-content\" id=\"artibody\">\n                        <p class=\"article-global\"></p>                            <p><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/cb9902ed9b6ec2e.jpg\"></p><p>目前的AirPods已经能够借助内置传感器实现空间音频头部追踪，而摄像头的加入或将进一步增强这一能力。系统代码显示，配备摄像头的AirPods可能会识别用户正在观看内容的实体屏幕，并将屏幕所处的方向与AirPods运动传感器推算出的头部朝向进行比对。</p><p>这款耳机预计能够识别笔记本电脑、显示器、智能手机、平板电脑和电视等设备。在用户同时使用多个显示器时，AirPods甚至可能判断用户当前注视的是哪一块屏幕，并将音频定位到对应设备。屏幕识别功能将会在后台运行，但当用户处于移动状态时，相关检测可能会暂时停止。</p><p>目前，配备Face ID的设备已经能够利用Face ID传感器辅助空间音频的头部追踪。如果用户同时佩戴带摄像头的AirPods，系统将优先采用耳机摄像头获取的信息，而不是Face ID传感器的数据。</p><p>系统代码还提到了基于服务器的视觉推理功能，这进一步强化了外界关于摄像头版AirPods将支持“视觉智能”的传闻。据称，当用户提出视觉智能相关请求时，AirPods会将摄像头采集的数据发送至苹果服务器进行处理。</p><p>今年8月发布的macOS Tahoe 26.7候选版本中，出现了大量尚未发布的苹果产品相关代码，其中就包括摄像头版AirPods。虽然系统内发现了多处与这款耳机有关的代码，但目前的传闻认为，苹果可能要到2027年秋季才会正式推出该产品。</p>                        </div>\n                    </div></body></html>","i":"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/cb9902ed9b6ec2e.jpg","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.cnbeta.com.tw/articles/tech/1575794.htm":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"article-content\" id=\"artibody\">\n                        <p class=\"article-global\"></p>                            <p><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/bd09c0bd1a30ad0.jpg\"></p><p>NeXT Dock于1988年随NeXTSTEP操作系统推出，是一种固定在屏幕上的应用图标栏，用户可以将常用程序放置其中，以便快速访问。它后来成为macOS Dock的直接前身，因此不少人认为，Windows 95任务栏可能是在借鉴NeXT Dock的基础上发展而来。</p><p><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/9d68f5bce413205.jpg\" title=\"\" alt=\"Windows-95-Start-menu.jpg\"></p><p>不过，微软前高级副总裁布拉德·西尔弗伯格和乔·贝尔菲奥雷都否认了这一说法。西尔弗伯格曾在上世纪90年代负责MS-DOS、Windows等产品。他表示，NeXT Dock与Windows 95任务栏存在明显差异，Windows 95任务栏是微软团队独立开发的，并非从NeXT Dock复制而来。他还称，自己曾与Windows 95用户界面设计师丹尼·奥兰讨论过此事，对方也确认任务栏设计来自自身构思，而不是借鉴NeXT。</p><p><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/ad3862cb6558498.jpg\" title=\"\" alt=\"OS-2.jpg\"></p><p>贝尔菲奥雷随后进一步解释，Windows 95任务栏的诞生主要受到两个因素影响，与NeXT Dock没有直接关系。</p><p><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/72f9b6f8e921711.jpg\" title=\"\" alt=\"Jeo-Belfiore-and-Brad-Silverberg-tell-who-designed-the-taskbar.jpg\"><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/0814aaf2ee68228.jpg\" title=\"\" alt=\"Brad-Silverberg-confirms-Windows-95-taskbar-was-not-taken-from-NeXT-Dock-e1788198629151.jpg\"></p><p>第一个因素是微软代号为Cairo的项目。Cairo于1991年至1996年间开发，目标是落实比尔·盖茨提出的“信息触手可及”理念。该项目最终没有作为独立操作系统发布，但其中许多技术和设计后来被逐步整合进微软其他产品。Cairo团队曾设计一条始终显示在屏幕底部的“托盘”，用于在不同应用程序之间拖放文件和内容。现有的Cairo桌面截图显示，这一设计早在Windows 95发布前多年就已经出现，并为后来任务栏的视觉形式提供了基础。</p><p>第二个因素则来自Windows 3.1的实际使用问题。贝尔菲奥雷表示，Windows 95需要一个专门放置最小化窗口的位置，这是对Windows 3.1遗留问题的解决。当时，用户一旦将程序最小化，就很难判断哪些程序仍在运行，也经常找不到已经打开的窗口。微软在可用性测试中反复发现这一问题，因此决定设计一个统一的界面，让用户能够查看并恢复最小化窗口。</p><p></p><p>任务栏按钮最初的主要作用并不是启动应用，而是恢复已经最小化的窗口。贝尔菲奥雷称，Windows 95希望通过一个统一的界面同时承载应用程序入口和窗口恢复功能，任务栏按钮正是为此产生的。至于利用任务栏按钮直接启动程序，则是多年以后才加入的功能。</p><p>到了Windows 7，微软将任务栏与此前的“快速启动”工具栏结合起来，允许用户把图标固定在任务栏中，即使相关应用尚未运行，图标也可以继续显示。从那时起，任务栏才真正同时具备窗口管理和应用启动功能。</p><p>任务栏的设计在Windows后续版本中仍不断变化。Windows 11于2021年发布时默认将任务栏图标置于屏幕中央，而且一度不允许用户把任务栏移动到其他边缘，引发了不少用户不满。微软后来承认，恢复任务栏位置调整功能需要重新处理大量依赖固定布局的应用程序，以避免任务栏移动后出现显示或交互问题。</p><p></p><p>随着微软重新承诺改善Windows质量，任务栏位置调整被列为重要改进内容。报道指出，微软已在今年恢复将任务栏移动到屏幕任意边缘的功能，使这一长期存在于Windows系统中的自定义选项重新面向所有用户开放，而不再仅限于Windows Insider测试人员。</p><p>因此，Windows 95任务栏并不是乔布斯NeXT Dock的衍生品。它更准确的来源，是微软Cairo项目中遗留下来的底部托盘设计，以及Windows 3.1时代用户难以追踪最小化窗口这一实际问题。</p>                        </div>\n                    </div></body></html>","i":"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/bd09c0bd1a30ad0.jpg","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.cnbeta.com.tw/articles/tech/1575792.htm":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"article-content\" id=\"artibody\">\n                        <p class=\"article-global\"></p>                            <p><a href=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0820/400810e5de4aa87.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0820/400810e5de4aa87.png\"></a></p><p>特朗普写道：“美国各地的社区如果不希望拥有数据中心，唯一的原因就是他们想要最终变得落后且贫穷。如果我们毁掉这只会下金蛋的鹅，能怪的只有我们自己。”</p><p>在11月中期选举临近之际，数据中心扩张已成为一个关键议题。多项民调显示，多数美国人反对在自己的社区建设数据中心。共和党和民主党人士都对这类项目表达担忧，议员和州政府领导人警告称，数据中心可能导致电网超负荷、供水系统承压，并带来严重噪声问题。</p><p>得克萨斯州共和党籍州长格雷格·阿博特本月出台了针对数据中心的新规定，尽管过去一年他在竞选活动中一直广泛支持数据中心建设。密歇根州共和党参议员候选人迈克·罗杰斯，以及宾夕法尼亚州共和党州长候选人斯泰西·加里蒂，也都呼吁暂缓部分数据中心项目。</p><p>美国副总统J·D·万斯周一在马里兰州安德鲁斯联合基地对记者表示：“我认为，数据中心引发的反弹，大概99%都发生在这样的地区：建设数据中心意味着当地居民要承担更高的公共事业费用和更高的电费。”</p><p>万斯提出，解决相关争议的办法之一，是要求建设数据中心的企业向电网回送电力。</p><p>他说：“如果你建设数据中心，就应该向电网输送电力，而不是从电网取走电力。如果能做到这一点，我认为数据中心就不会引发太大争议。真正的问题在于，当居民的公用事业账单大幅上涨时，情况就变得严重了。”</p><p>不过，特朗普仍坚持认为，数据中心对于美国在人工智能竞赛中保持对中国的领先地位至关重要。特朗普近期接受其前私人顾问迈克尔·科恩采访时曾表达这一观点，并于周一再次重申。</p><p>特朗普还写道：“中国不可能不为这场反数据中心运动感到高兴。事实上，他们简直不敢相信这种事情正在发生！”</p><p>这并不是特朗普第一次推动数据中心扩张。去年，他签署行政命令，要求加快数据中心的审批和建设。在今年7月的另一篇“真实社交”平台帖文中，他称数据中心是“未来就业的最大推动力量之一”。</p><p>纽约州今年7月成为美国第一个暂停新基础设施建设的州。民主党籍州长凯西·霍楚尔签署相关行政命令后不久，特朗普便对此举提出批评。</p>                        </div>\n                    </div></body></html>","i":"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0820/400810e5de4aa87.png","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.mac52ipod.cn/post/apple-pay-transit-card-support-zhengzhou.php":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"textbox-content\" id=\"zoomtext\"><p>\n\t \tApple Pay 公交支持刷郑州绿城通交通卡了。苹果用户可以在郑州乘坐公交、地铁时直接刷手机或手表，Appley Pay 使用的 NFC 方案只需手机往读卡器上一靠，比扫二维码方便得多。</p><p>其实，Apple Pay 早就通过互联互通卡支持全国几百个城市的公交卡了。但支持本地公交卡有助于用户享受本地公交优惠。比如这次郑州绿城通交通卡给出了公交车 8 折和地铁 9.5 折优惠。</p><p>而且这次新增的也是互联互通卡，到开通一卡通互联的其它 300 多个中国城市也能用。</p><p>iPhone XS、iPhone XS Max、iPhone XR 或更新机型用户，可以将公交卡设为「快捷交通卡」，手机没电自动关机 5 小时内依然可以刷交通卡。所以不用担心「上车后手机没电，没法下车/出站」。注意是自动关机，你长按电源键手动关机就不能刷卡出站了。</p><p>更多开卡方式、城市列表、支持设备等信息，看苹果中国官网关于 Apple Pay 公交卡的详细介绍吧 <u><a href=\"https://www.apple.com.cn/apple-pay/transit/\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"苹果中国官网\" rel=\"nofollow\"><font>https://www.apple.com.cn/apple-pay/transit/</font></a></u></p><p><a name=\"entrymore\"></a>\n</p>\n\t<p class=\"textbox-bottom\">\n\t</p>\n\t\n</div>\n</div></body></html>","i":"","t":"2026-09-02","p":"","n":0},"https://www.cnbeta.com.tw/articles/movie/1575790.htm":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"article-content\" id=\"artibody\">\n                        <p class=\"article-global\"></p>                            <p><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/bd6f3c489c4bc58.webp\"></p><p>频道内容涵盖电影、电视剧、动漫、新闻、体育、纪录片等多个类别。电影频道包括由狮门影业推出的MovieSphere、50 Cent Action，以及Sony One Horror Hits等，覆盖动作、科幻和恐怖题材。电视剧方面，用户可以观看《废柴联盟》《行尸走肉》《美国版一掷千金》《恐惧因素》和《冰路卡车》等节目。</p><p>动漫内容则包括《火影忍者》《美少女战士》《全职猎人》和《死亡笔记》等作品。此外，平台还将提供游戏、电子竞技、播客和喜剧类节目频道。考虑到索尼旗下拥有Crunchyroll，动漫内容的加入也并不令人意外。</p><p>索尼表示，PS5上的直播电视服务将持续更新节目内容，并陆续加入新的频道。公司还计划未来把这项服务扩展到加拿大及其他地区。</p><p></p><p>从商业角度来看，这项举措对索尼而言具有一定合理性。继基本停止生产游戏光盘等近期业务决策之后，索尼希望推动主机用户直接在PS5上观看FAST频道，而不是转向Pluto、Roku或Tubi等其他平台。这样既能让用户更多地停留在PlayStation生态中，也可能为索尼带来额外收入。当前，索尼正越来越重视从现有客户身上获得更多收益，而不是单纯依赖向新用户销售PS5主机。</p><p>不过，这项服务推出的时机至少算不上理想。围绕游戏光盘贬值问题的反弹短期内仍难以平息。索尼最近还告知欧洲用户，由于授权协议到期，他们将失去在PlayStation Store上购买的数百部电影的访问权限。</p><p>当然，PlayStation仍有更多游戏正在开发中，索尼也将在本周举行的两场State of Play活动中展示其中一部分作品。但从目前的表现来看，这项新服务更像是在把PS5推向Xbox One曾经尝试过的方向。微软当年曾将Xbox One定位为一体化娱乐中心，但这一战略最终并未取得成功。</p>                        </div>\n                    </div></body></html>","i":"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/bd6f3c489c4bc58.webp","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.cnbeta.com.tw/articles/game/1575788.htm":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"article-content\" id=\"artibody\">\n                        <p class=\"article-global\"></p>                            <p><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/bd1a66638378b1f.jpg\"></p><p>从平台表现来看，PlayStation 5贡献了此次增长的绝大部分。8月27日当天，PS5版预购量增长606%；相比之下，Xbox Series X|S版预购量仅增长127%。自Sensor Tower于今年6月开始追踪《GTA 6》预购情况以来，PS5的预购量就一直领先于Xbox。该追踪工作始于Rockstar正式开放游戏预购后不久。</p><p>Sensor Tower目前估计，《GTA 6》全球累计预购量约为486万份，对应金额接近4.76亿美元。其中，PlayStation平台购买者约占总量的77%。</p><p>Take-Two尚未确认具体销售数据。不过，公司首席执行官施特劳斯·泽尔尼克此前曾表示，售价100美元的终极版需求已经超过售价80美元的标准版。自《GTA 6》早期预告片发布以来，Rockstar一直严格控制实机内容的公开节奏，因此，这段长达26分钟的展示视频对预购数据产生显著推动并不意外。</p><p>Sensor Tower分析师还指出，当前不同版本之间的购买比例未必会一直保持不变。随着游戏临近发售，大量普通消费者开始进行预购，终极版与标准版的占比可能再次发生变化，相关平台和版本比例也可能在正式上市前继续调整。</p><p><img src=\"https://www.techpowerup.com/img/PDhvGmJsu0MPZ693.jpg\"></p>                        </div>\n                    </div></body></html>","i":"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/bd1a66638378b1f.jpg","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.cnbeta.com.tw/articles/science/1575786.htm":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"article-content\" id=\"artibody\">\n                        <p class=\"article-global\"></p>                            <p><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/d9fb934882a1175.webp\"></p><p>几年前，老挝一家背包客旅舍曾发生甲醇中毒事件，导致6名外国游客死亡。2025年，土耳其也发生了更大规模的假酒中毒事件，造成160人死亡，超过250人留下不同程度的身体损伤。这两起事件均被认为与饮用非法生产的甲醇污染酒精有关。</p><p>甲醇造成的危害之所以令人担忧，还在于只需极少剂量就可能引发严重后果。约10毫升甲醇，也就是两茶匙的量，便可能导致永久性失明和肾衰竭；摄入更多则可能致命。</p><p>日常生活中常见的酒精主要有三种：存在于酒类饮品中的乙醇、用于消毒和清洁的异丙醇，以及用于挡风玻璃清洗液、防冻剂和溶剂的工业化学品甲醇。只有乙醇适合饮用，但一些假酒生产者会用甲醇稀释乙醇。这样做可能是因为甲醇能够制造酒精度更高的假象，不像饮用酒精那样需要缴税，而且价格低廉，能够提高利润。</p><p>正规酒类生产商通常采用严格的质量控制体系，所有产品都要经过广泛检测。这类检测不仅成本高，也需要较长时间。在苏格兰圣安德鲁斯大学和澳大利亚南澳大利亚州阿德莱德大学的科学家取得一项最新成果之前，人们还无法在不开启酒瓶、不将样品送往实验室的情况下完成相关检测。</p><p>研究人员采用了一种名为拉曼光谱的技术，用来读取他们所说的“液体独特的化学指纹”。其原理是将激光束照射到液体中，再分析光线撞击液体表面并激发液体分子后产生的散射变化。不同液体会形成不同的光谱特征，而这些特征能够揭示液体的化学成分。</p><p>通过精确调整激光束的形状并改变其波长，研究人员成功滤除了酒瓶本身造成的干扰。因此，这种检测方法无需打开瓶子，成为该研究最重要的突破之一。</p><p>研究团队在威士忌中检测出了甲醇，其检测浓度约为国际公认安全标准的十分之一。在具备极高可靠性的同时，这项技术还比传统实验室检测更便宜、更快速，因此有望成为全球打击假酒的重要工具。</p><p>澳大利亚等葡萄酒生产大国或许能从中大幅受益，因为葡萄酒造假每年都会给全球产业造成数十亿美元的损失。不过，这种方法的应用潜力远不止于酒类行业。研究人员希望未来能利用它鉴别假冒香水、检测橄榄油中的农药污染，并进一步提升整个农业领域的质量控制水平。</p><p>这项新技术目前主要面向海关机构、酒类生产商和经销商，以及食品安全监管部门等大型组织。它或许能够降低假酒流入商店货架的风险，但消费者仍然可能受到威胁。避开价格异常低廉的酒类，以及标签信息不完整或不规范的产品，仍是消费者保护自己的有效方式。</p>                        </div>\n                    </div></body></html>","i":"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/d9fb934882a1175.webp","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.cnbeta.com.tw/articles/tech/1575784.htm":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"article-content\" id=\"artibody\">\n                        <p class=\"article-global\"></p>                            <p><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/d70ade2f61ef519.jpg\"></p><p>目前，新闻稿仍保留“新一代固态硬盘架构”的描述，并称其存储速度最高可达到上一代的两倍，但不再提及 PCIe 6.0。苹果尚未回应相关置评请求，不过从目前情况来看，这很可能只是新闻稿中的一处错误，因为新款 Mac Studio 更有可能支持 PCIe 5.0 标准。</p><p>首先，搭载同款 M5 Max 芯片的 14 英寸和 16 英寸 MacBook Pro 已经采用 PCIe 5.0 固态硬盘，苹果同样宣称这些笔记本的固态硬盘速度最高可提升至上一代的两倍。其次，目前市场上还没有任何消费级电脑配备支持 PCIe 6.0 的固态硬盘。</p><p>虽然 M5 Ultra 芯片是全新产品，但它很可能同样支持 PCIe 5.0，否则苹果没有必要修改 Mac Studio 的新闻稿。</p><p>综合来看，新款 Mac Studio 似乎支持的是 PCIe 5.0，而不是 PCIe 6.0。</p>                        </div>\n                    </div></body></html>","i":"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/d70ade2f61ef519.jpg","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.cnbeta.com.tw/articles/tech/1575782.htm":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"article-content\" id=\"artibody\">\n                        <p class=\"article-global\"></p>                            <p><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/97a2ca541994c8a.jpg\"></p><p>这三款设备此前属于“老旧产品”。按照苹果的相关规定，产品停止销售五年后会进入老旧产品名单，达到七年后则会被列为过时产品。老旧产品在苹果零售店和授权服务商处仍可能获得维修，但前提是当地仍有可用零件；过时产品通常不再享有维修或硬件服务，苹果也会停止生产相关维修部件。</p><p>不过，苹果对Mac笔记本提供最长十年的电池专项维修政策，期限从产品最后一次销售起计算。因此，2017款和2018款MacBook Pro，以及2018款MacBook Air的用户，未来仍有机会获得电池更换服务，具体情况取决于设备型号、地区及零件供应。</p><p>2018款MacBook Air是MacBook Air产品线中首款配备Touch ID和视网膜显示屏的机型。相比此前采用非视网膜屏幕的MacBook Air，它拥有更高分辨率和更鲜艳的色彩。同年，苹果还重新设计了MacBook Air，缩窄了屏幕边框，并采用更薄、更轻的机身。</p><p>2017款MacBook Pro主要升级为英特尔Kaby Lake处理器，其他方面变化相对有限。2018款更新机型则首次支持原彩显示，并搭载第三代蝶式键盘。</p>                        </div>\n                    </div></body></html>","i":"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/97a2ca541994c8a.jpg","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.cnbeta.com.tw/articles/tech/1575780.htm":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"article-content\" id=\"artibody\">\n                        <p class=\"article-global\"></p>                            <p>作者：克里斯・莫里斯</p><p><img src=\"https://n.sinaimg.cn/finance/transform/59/w550h309/20260901/a11c-562460f4c320b12515c3a24f41f7299c.png\" alt=\"\"><br></p><p>她的同伙凯丽卡・沃瑟姆已于 2023 年被判处同样 16 年刑期。今年 3 月，沃瑟姆因承认伪造联邦法官签名，刑期又被追加一年。法院同时判令两人向亚马逊赔偿 946 万 9731.45 美元，她们名下的房产与车辆均被没收。</p><p>美国司法部称，哈德逊今年 3 月经陪审团裁定，共计 30 项重罪成立，且<strong>不得获得假释</strong>。</p><p>美国联邦检察官西奥多・S・赫茨伯格在声明中表示：“哈德逊及其同伙策划了一场针对亚马逊的特大诈骗，短短数月之内就盗取近 1000 万美元。 哈德逊在取保候审期间，还伪造联邦法官签名，企图再诈骗另一家公司，此举充分体现她对法律的全然藐视。今天这份重判…… 是对她一连串犯罪行为的追责。”</p><p><strong>“贪欲彻底失控”</strong></p><p>调查机关认定哈德逊是这一系列犯罪的主谋。她经营一家为亚马逊派送包裹的公司，与沃瑟姆是恋人关系；沃瑟姆任职于亚特兰大郊外的亚马逊仓库，担任运营经理。</p><p>据官方披露，2022 年 1‑6 月，二人使用虚假发票，在亚马逊供应商系统内录入虚假供应商账号。沃瑟姆凭借岗位权限，可以审批新增供应商以及发票付款。最终，哈德逊与沃瑟姆提交了 1000 余份虚假发票，全部由沃瑟姆审批通过。</p><p>据报道，诈骗得来的赃款被用来购置一套价值 100 万美元的住宅以及多辆豪车，包括一台 2019 款兰博基尼 Urus、一台 2018 款保时捷帕拉梅拉。二人于 2022 年 9 月被提起刑事指控。</p><p>美国特勤局在今年早些时候公布哈德逊定罪结果时评价，这是一起 “只能用贪欲彻底失控来形容” 的案件。</p><p><strong>罪行变本加厉</strong></p><p>司法部表示，在取保候审阶段，两人还试图诈骗一家特许经营企业。她们向一家水烟馆经营者谎称，针对她们的亚马逊相关指控已经撤销；同时发送篡改过的财务报表，还附上伪造签名的法院文书，仿冒签名包括联邦地区法院前首席法官蒂莫西・C・巴滕、以及本案当时的检察官科布县治安法官诺曼・L・巴尼特。</p><p>美国特勤局在领英发文评论：“联邦案件还悬而未决，做出这种事实在算不上明智之举。”</p>                        </div>\n                    </div></body></html>","i":"https://n.sinaimg.cn/finance/transform/59/w550h309/20260901/a11c-562460f4c320b12515c3a24f41f7299c.png","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.cnbeta.com.tw/articles/tech/1575778.htm":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"article-content\" id=\"artibody\">\n                        <p class=\"article-global\"></p>                            <p><img src=\"https://www.techpowerup.com/img/EZL7KmH8sVPDdgfw.jpg\"></p><p><img src=\"https://www.techpowerup.com/img/Q96NqMCRt9Vz6XNH.jpg\"></p><p><img src=\"https://www.techpowerup.com/img/DhhmwezNPo8dYHlw.jpg\"></p><p>YouTube频道UFD Tech使用SSD写入测试工具进行了测试。结果显示，256GB版MacBook Neo在写入20TB数据后，预计已经消耗约5%的整体寿命，据此推算其额定写入寿命约为414TB；512GB版本的预计额定寿命则约为1521TB。<br></p><p>随后，该频道主持人Brett连续使用MacBook Neo一天，以估算设备在内存不足时，交换文件每天会向SSD写入多少数据。测试期间，他主要将这台笔记本当作网络终端使用，包括通过Chrome进行资料查找、阅读和通信，并运行WhatsApp与Discord。结果显示，仅仅使用三个小时，MacBook Neo就向SSD写入了“接近900GB”的数据。</p><p>如果按照MacBook Neo约400至420TB的预估耐久度计算，那么在全天候承担基础办公任务的情况下，其SSD预计只能持续约1400小时，也就是58天左右。相对而言，MacBook Neo的512GB SSD似乎拥有256GB版本约2至3倍的耐久度，在持续使用的情况下，预计可以运行约5000小时后才达到额定写入上限。</p><p></p><p>当然，实际结果会因用户的使用方式而存在很大差异，SSD标称寿命也不能完全等同于硬盘真正能够使用的时间。不过，这项测试确实引发了外界对苹果依赖交换机制的担忧，尤其是在设备内存容量受到限制的情况下。</p><p>更令人担忧的是，MacBook Neo搭载的SSD无法更换。当SSD最终耗尽全部写入周期后，维修成本可能高于直接购买一块新硬盘，而且还可能伴随数据丢失风险。</p><p>苹果似乎也意识到内存容量是MacBook Neo最薄弱的环节。近期一直有传闻称，苹果可能在不久后为该产品改用A19 Pro芯片，并将内存容量从8GB提升至12GB。</p>                        </div>\n                    </div></body></html>","i":"https://www.techpowerup.com/img/EZL7KmH8sVPDdgfw.jpg","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.cnbeta.com.tw/articles/tech/1575776.htm":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"article-content\" id=\"artibody\">\n                        <p class=\"article-global\"></p>                            <p><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/685b1349f62238f.jpg\"></p><p>对于年轻用户而言，MapQuest曾经是一项广受欢迎的地图服务。在智能手机以及Google地图、Apple Maps等应用出现之前，人们经常会为公路旅行打印纸质路线，因此MapQuest一度十分流行。</p><p>如今，MapQuest仍提供iOS和Android应用，但其知名度早已不及巅峰时期。不过，这一情况最近似乎出现了变化。MapQuest当天宣布，自上周四以来，已有数十万人下载其应用。截至8月30日，该公司地图服务的使用量约增长了50倍。</p><p></p><p>MapQuest总经理道格·伯杰在新闻稿中表示：“我们采取了与处理墨西哥湾名称时相同的方法：参与这场讨论，并为用户提供一款继续保留他们熟悉名称的应用。”</p><p>他说：“本周末有数十万人下载我们的应用，这向我们表明，我们做出了正确的选择。”</p><p>目前，Google地图已向美国用户显示“美国湖”这一名称，但苹果尚未采取相同做法。</p>                        </div>\n                    </div></body></html>","i":"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/685b1349f62238f.jpg","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.cnbeta.com.tw/articles/movie/1575774.htm":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"article-content\" id=\"artibody\">\n                        <p class=\"article-global\"></p>                            <p>就在2025年1月，VLC的下载量刚刚突破60亿次，距今约18个月后又增加了10亿次下载。</p><p>肯普夫表示，VideoLAN近期已将VLC移植到亚马逊面向电视设备推出的新操作系统Vega OS。该组织还称，团队正在努力支持其他平台和编解码器，同时为VLC 4版本进行开发。不过，这一版本的研发进度较为缓慢，仍需要一定时间。</p><p>去年，VideoLAN曾预告将利用本地模型推出人工智能翻译和字幕功能，但目前尚不清楚这些功能是否已经正式发布。</p><p><a href=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2024/0323/561deda35d54b2d.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2024/0323/561deda35d54b2d.jpg\"></a></p>                        </div>\n                    </div></body></html>","i":"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2024/0323/561deda35d54b2d.jpg","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.cnbeta.com.tw/articles/tech/1575772.htm":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"article-content\" id=\"artibody\">\n                        <p class=\"article-global\"></p>                            <p>据彭博社援引知情人士消息称，他是在Tim Cook担任苹果首席执行官的最后几天作出这一决定的。苹果目前尚未正式对外公布相关调整。</p><p>虽然席勒不再负责App Store和产品活动，但他暂时不会离开苹果。据悉，他已向员工表示，接下来将转而参与一些尚未公开的项目。</p><p>此次职责变化被视为席勒逐步淡出苹果日常管理、并可能走向退休的又一步。2020年他转任苹果院士时，格雷格·乔斯维亚克接替了他的全球营销高级副总裁职位。席勒当时曾表示，新的工作安排能让他有更多时间陪伴朋友和家人，并投入几个自己非常重视的个人项目。</p><p>随着席勒不再参与App Store及苹果活动的日常运营，他或许将拥有更多时间处理个人事务，同时继续以顾问或其他形式参与公司工作。</p><p>席勒职责调整的时间点也颇为敏感。相关消息曝光当天正是库克担任苹果首席执行官的最后一天，约翰·特努斯将于周二正式接任公司掌门人。尽管目前没有迹象表明席勒的决定与苹果首席执行官交接直接相关，但两件事在时间上恰好重合。</p><p>近期苹果高层已经出现多项变化，虽然尚未形成大规模管理层离职潮，但公司整体运营方式可能随领导层交接而发生调整。App Store仍是苹果生态体系和业务版图中的重要组成部分，苹果预计不会长期让这一职责处于无人负责的状态。</p><p><img src=\"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/9a617e43fbdc9b2.jpg\"></p>                        </div>\n                    </div></body></html>","i":"https://static.cnbetacdn.com/article/2026/0901/9a617e43fbdc9b2.jpg","t":"2026-08-31","p":"","n":0},"https://www.v2ex.com/t/1238661":{"c":"<div class=\"topic_content\"><div class=\"markdown_body\"><p>ç›®å‰�å­˜æ¬¾å¤§æ¦‚ 80 ä¸ªå·¦å�³ï¼Œæ¯•ä¸š 6 å¹´äº†ï¼Œæœ€è¿‘åœ¨ç�¢ç£¨ä¹°è½¦çš„äº‹æƒ…ï¼Œåœ¨çœ‹å°�ç±³ su7 ï¼Œä¸»è¦�æ˜¯åˆ°åº•ä¹°ä¸�ä¹°ã€‚\nç›®å‰�è‡ªå·±çš„æƒ…å†µï¼š<br/>\nå·¥ä½œé€šå‹¤å�¯ä»¥åœ°é“�ç›´è¾¾ï¼ŒåŸºæœ¬ä¸�éœ€è¦�å¼€è½¦ï¼Œå…¬å�¸ä¹Ÿåœ¨åœ°é